    // web-security/cross-site-scripting
    'In this section, we\'ll explain what cross-site scripting is, describe the different varieties of cross-site scripting vulnerabilities, and spell out how to find and prevent cross-site scripting.' => 'Pada bagian ini dijelaskan apa itu cross-site scripting, berbagai jenis kerentanannya, serta cara menemukan dan mencegah XSS.',
    'What is cross-site scripting (XSS)?' => 'Apa itu cross-site scripting (XSS)?',
    'Cross-site scripting (also known as XSS) is a web security vulnerability that allows an attacker to compromise the interactions that users have with a vulnerable application. It allows an attacker to circumvent the same origin policy, which is designed to segregate different websites from each other. Cross-site scripting vulnerabilities normally allow an attacker to masquerade as a victim user, to carry out any actions that the user is able to perform, and to access any of the user\'s data. If the victim user has privileged access within the application, then the attacker might be able to gain full control over all of the application\'s functionality and data.' => 'Cross-site scripting (XSS) adalah kerentanan keamanan web yang memungkinkan penyerang memanipulasi interaksi pengguna dengan aplikasi yang rentan. Celah ini membuat penyerang mampu melewati same-origin policy yang seharusnya mengisolasi satu situs dari situs lain. Dengan XSS, penyerang biasanya dapat menyamar sebagai korban, melakukan aksi apa pun yang dimiliki korban, dan mengakses seluruh data milik korban. Jika korban memegang hak akses istimewa, penyerang berpotensi mengambil alih kendali penuh aplikasi.',
    'Cross-site scripting works by manipulating a vulnerable web site so that it returns malicious JavaScript to users. When the malicious code executes inside a victim\'s browser, the attacker can fully compromise their interaction with the application.' => 'Cross-site scripting bekerja dengan memanipulasi situs yang rentan agar mengirimkan JavaScript berbahaya ke browser pengguna. Begitu skrip berjalan di sisi korban, penyerang dapat membajak seluruh interaksi pengguna pada aplikasi.',
    'If you\'re already familiar with the basic concepts behind XSS vulnerabilities and just want to practice exploiting them on some realistic, deliberately vulnerable targets, you can access all of the labs in this topic from the link below.' => 'Jika Anda sudah memahami konsep dasar kerentanan XSS dan ingin langsung mempraktikkannya pada target latihan, akses seluruh lab topik ini melalui tautan berikut.',
    'XSS proof of concept' => 'Bukti konsep (PoC) XSS',
    'You can confirm most kinds of XSS vulnerability by injecting a payload that causes your own browser to execute some arbitrary JavaScript. It\'s long been common practice to use the [[C0]] function for this purpose because it\'s short, harmless, and pretty hard to miss when it\'s successfully called. In fact, you solve the majority of our XSS labs by invoking [[C1]] in a simulated victim\'s browser.' => 'Sebagian besar kerentanan XSS dapat dibuktikan dengan menyisipkan payload yang mengeksekusi JavaScript sembarang di browser. Sudah lama fungsi [[C0]] dipakai untuk bukti konsep karena singkat, aman, dan mudah terlihat saat terpanggil. Mayoritas lab XSS di akademi ini diselesaikan dengan memicu [[C1]] pada browser korban simulasi.',
    'Unfortunately, there\'s a slight hitch if you use Chrome. From version 92 onward (July 20th, 2021), cross-origin iframes are prevented from calling [[C0]]. As these are used to construct some of the more advanced XSS attacks, you\'ll sometimes need to use an alternative PoC payload. In this scenario, we recommend the [[C1]] function. If you\'re interested in learning more about this change and why we like [[C2]], [[A0]]check out our blog post[[/A0]] on the subject.' => 'Namun mulai Chrome versi 92 ke atas, iframe cross-origin dicegah memanggil [[C0]]. Karena iframe semacam itu sering dipakai pada skenario XSS lanjutan, terkadang diperlukan fungsi PoC alternatif seperti [[C1]]. Informasi lengkap mengenai perubahan ini tersedia di [[A0]]catatan riset kami[[/A0]].',
    'As the simulated victim in our labs uses Chrome, we\'ve amended the affected labs so that they can also be solved using [[C0]]. We\'ve indicated this in the instructions wherever relevant.' => 'Karena browser korban simulasi menggunakan mesin Chromium modern, lab terkait juga dapat diselesaikan dengan [[C0]], seperti yang tertulis pada masing-masing petunjuk lab.',
    'What are the types of XSS attacks?' => 'Apa saja jenis serangan XSS?',
    'There are three main types of XSS attacks. These are:' => 'Ada tiga jenis utama serangan XSS:',
    '[[A0]]Reflected XSS[[/A0]], where the malicious script comes from the current HTTP request.' => '[[A0]]Reflected XSS[[/A0]], ketika skrip berbahaya berasal langsung dari permintaan HTTP saat ini.',
    '[[A0]]Stored XSS[[/A0]], where the malicious script comes from the website\'s database.' => '[[A0]]Stored XSS[[/A0]], ketika skrip berbahaya tersimpan di database situs lalu ditampilkan kemudian.',
    '[[A0]]DOM-based XSS[[/A0]], where the vulnerability exists in client-side code rather than server-side code.' => '[[A0]]DOM-based XSS[[/A0]], ketika kerentanan berada di kode JavaScript sisi klien ketimbang kode server.',
    'Reflected cross-site scripting' => 'Reflected cross-site scripting',
    'Reflected XSS is the simplest variety of cross-site scripting. It arises when an application receives data in an HTTP request and includes that data within the immediate response in an unsafe way.' => 'Reflected XSS adalah varian XSS paling sederhana. Celah ini muncul saat aplikasi menerima data dari permintaan HTTP lalu langsung menyisipkannya ke dalam respons tanpa pengamanan.',
    'Here is a simple example of a reflected XSS vulnerability:' => 'Berikut contoh sederhana kerentanan reflected XSS:',
    'The application doesn\'t perform any other processing of the data, so an attacker can easily construct an attack like this:' => 'Karena aplikasi tidak menyaring atau meng-encode data tersebut, penyerang dapat merakit URL eksploitasi seperti ini:',
    'If the user visits the URL constructed by the attacker, then the attacker\'s script executes in the user\'s browser, in the context of that user\'s session with the application. At that point, the script can carry out any action, and retrieve any data, to which the user has access.' => 'Saat korban membuka URL buatan penyerang, skrip berbahaya berjalan di browser korban dalam konteks sesi login korban, sehingga mampu melakukan aksi dan membaca data apa pun milik korban.',
    'Cross-site scripting cheat sheet' => 'Contekan cross-site scripting (XSS)',
    'Stored cross-site scripting' => 'Stored cross-site scripting',
    'Stored XSS (also known as persistent or second-order XSS) arises when an application receives data from an untrusted source and includes that data within its later HTTP responses in an unsafe way.' => 'Stored XSS (sering disebut persistent atau second-order XSS) terjadi saat aplikasi menerima data dari sumber luar lalu menampilkannya di respons HTTP berikutnya tanpa pengamanan.',
    'The data in question might be submitted to the application via HTTP requests; for example, comments on a blog post, user nicknames in a chat room, or contact details on a customer order. In other cases, the data might arrive from other untrusted sources; for example, a webmail application displaying messages received over SMTP, a marketing application displaying social media posts, or a network monitoring application displaying packet data from network traffic.' => 'Data tersebut bisa masuk lewat permintaan HTTP, seperti komentar blog, nama tampilan di ruang obrolan, atau detail kontak pesanan. Data juga bisa berasal dari sumber eksternal lain, seperti pesan email di aplikasi webmail, unggahan media sosial di dasbor pemasaran, atau log paket jaringan pada alat pemantau.',
    'Here is a simple example of a stored XSS vulnerability. A message board application lets users submit messages, which are displayed to other users:' => 'Berikut contoh sederhana stored XSS pada papan pesan yang menampilkan kiriman pengguna ke pengguna lain:',
    'The application doesn\'t perform any other processing of the data, so an attacker can easily send a message that attacks other users:' => 'Karena isi pesan tidak disaring saat disimpan maupun ditampilkan, penyerang cukup mengirim pesan berisi skrip untuk menyerang pengguna lain:',
    'DOM-based XSS (also known as DOM XSS) arises when an application contains some client-side JavaScript that processes data from an untrusted source in an unsafe way, usually by writing the data back to the DOM.' => 'DOM-based XSS (DOM XSS) muncul ketika kode JavaScript sisi klien memproses data dari sumber yang bisa dikendalikan pengguna secara tidak aman, biasanya dengan menuliskannya kembali ke dalam DOM.',
    'In the following example, an application uses some JavaScript to read the value from an input field and write that value to an element within the HTML:' => 'Pada contoh berikut, JavaScript membaca nilai kolom input lalu menuliskannya langsung ke elemen HTML:',
    'If the attacker can control the value of the input field, they can easily construct a malicious value that causes their own script to execute:' => 'Bila nilai input dapat dikendalikan penyerang, payload dapat dibuat agar langsung menjalankan JavaScript:',
    'In a typical case, the input field would be populated from part of the HTTP request, such as a URL query string parameter, allowing the attacker to deliver an attack using a malicious URL, in the same manner as reflected XSS.' => 'Dalam praktiknya, nilai input kerap diisi dari parameter query string URL, sehingga penyerang dapat mengirimkan serangan cukup lewat tautan berbahaya seperti pada reflected XSS.',
    'What can XSS be used for?' => 'Apa saja yang dapat dilakukan lewat XSS?',
    'An attacker who exploits a cross-site scripting vulnerability is typically able to:' => 'Penyerang yang berhasil mengeksploitasi XSS umumnya mampu:',
    'Impersonate or masquerade as the victim user.' => 'Menyamar sebagai pengguna korban.',
    'Carry out any action that the user is able to perform.' => 'Melakukan aksi apa pun yang diizinkan bagi korban.',
    'Read any data that the user is able to access.' => 'Membaca seluruh data yang bisa diakses oleh korban.',
    'Capture the user\'s login credentials.' => 'Mencuri kredensial login pengguna.',
    'Perform virtual defacement of the web site.' => 'Mengubah tampilan halaman situs secara virtual.',
    'Inject trojan functionality into the web site.' => 'Menyisipkan skrip trojan ke dalam halaman web.',
    'Impact of XSS vulnerabilities' => 'Dampak kerentanan XSS',
    'The actual impact of an XSS attack generally depends on the nature of the application, its functionality and data, and the status of the compromised user. For example:' => 'Besar kecilnya dampak XSS bergantung pada sifat aplikasi, sensitivitas data, serta hak akses pengguna yang terkena serangan. Contohnya:',
    'In a brochureware application, where all users are anonymous and all information is public, the impact will often be minimal.' => 'Pada situs informasi publik yang seluruh kontennya terbuka dan tanpa login, dampaknya relatif kecil.',
    'In an application holding sensitive data, such as banking transactions, emails, or healthcare records, the impact will usually be serious.' => 'Pada aplikasi yang menyimpan transaksi perbankan, email, atau rekam medis, dampaknya tergolong serius.',
    'If the compromised user has elevated privileges within the application, then the impact will generally be critical, allowing the attacker to take full control of the vulnerable application and compromise all users and their data.' => 'Jika korban memiliki hak administrator, dampaknya kritis karena penyerang dapat menguasai aplikasi dan seluruh data penggunanya.',
    'Exploiting cross-site scripting vulnerabilities' => 'Mengeksploitasi kerentanan cross-site scripting',
    'How to find and test for XSS vulnerabilities' => 'Cara menemukan dan menguji kerentanan XSS',
    'The vast majority of XSS vulnerabilities can be found quickly and reliably using Burp Suite\'s web vulnerability scanner.' => 'Sebagian besar kerentanan XSS dapat dideteksi dengan cepat dan konsisten menggunakan pemindai kerentanan web.',
    'Manually testing for reflected and stored XSS normally involves submitting some simple unique input (such as a short alphanumeric string) into every entry point in the application, identifying every location where the submitted input is returned in HTTP responses, and testing each location individually to determine whether suitably crafted input can be used to execute arbitrary JavaScript. In this way, you can determine the [[A0]]context[[/A0]] in which the XSS occurs and select a suitable payload to exploit it.' => 'Pengujian manual untuk reflected dan stored XSS biasanya dilakukan dengan mengirim string alfanumerik unik ke setiap titik input, menelusuri lokasi kemunculannya di respons HTTP, lalu menguji tiap lokasi guna menentukan [[A0]]konteks XSS[[/A0]] dan payload yang sesuai.',
    'Manually testing for DOM-based XSS arising from URL parameters involves a similar process: placing some simple unique input in the parameter, using the browser\'s developer tools to search the DOM for this input, and testing each location to determine whether it is exploitable. However, other types of DOM XSS are harder to detect. To find DOM-based vulnerabilities in non-URL-based input (such as [[C0]]) or non-HTML-based sinks (like [[C1]]), there is no substitute for reviewing JavaScript code, which can be extremely time-consuming. Burp Suite\'s web vulnerability scanner combines static and dynamic analysis of JavaScript to reliably automate the detection of DOM-based vulnerabilities.' => 'Pengujian DOM XSS dari parameter URL memakai pola serupa dengan mencari string unik di DOM lewat Developer Tools browser. Namun untuk sumber non-URL seperti [[C0]] atau sink selain HTML seperti [[C1]], diperlukan tinjauan kode JavaScript atau kombinasi analisis statis dan dinamis otomatis.',
    'Cross-site scripting contexts' => 'Konteks cross-site scripting',
    'Content security policy' => 'Content Security Policy',
    'Content security policy (CSP) is a browser mechanism that aims to mitigate the impact of cross-site scripting and some other vulnerabilities. If an application that employs CSP contains XSS-like behavior, then the CSP might hinder or prevent exploitation of the vulnerability. Often, the CSP can be circumvented to enable exploitation of the underlying vulnerability.' => 'Content Security Policy (CSP) adalah mekanisme keamanan browser untuk membatasi dampak XSS dan sejumlah serangan lain. Jika aplikasi memiliki celah XSS namun menerapkan CSP, kebijakan tersebut dapat menghambat atau memblokir eksekusi payload, walau kebijakan yang longgar sering masih bisa diakali.',
    'Dangling markup injection is a technique that can be used to capture data cross-domain in situations where a full cross-site scripting exploit is not possible, due to input filters or other defenses. It can often be exploited to capture sensitive information that is visible to other users, including CSRF tokens that can be used to perform unauthorized actions on behalf of the user.' => 'Injeksi dangling markup adalah teknik pencurian data lintas domain ketika eksploitasi XSS penuh terhalang filter atau CSP. Teknik ini sering dipakai untuk membocorkan token CSRF atau data sensitif yang tampil pada halaman pengguna lain.',
    'Preventing cross-site scripting is trivial in some cases but can be much harder depending on the complexity of the application and the ways it handles user-controllable data.' => 'Pencegahan XSS terkadang cukup mudah, namun bisa menjadi rumit pada aplikasi kompleks dengan banyak alur pengolahan input pengguna.',
    'In general, effectively preventing XSS vulnerabilities is likely to involve a combination of the following measures:' => 'Secara umum, pencegahan XSS yang efektif menggabungkan langkah-langkah berikut:',
    '<strong>Filter input on arrival.</strong> At the point where user input is received, filter as strictly as possible based on what is expected or valid input.' => '<strong>Saring input saat diterima.</strong> Lakukan validasi seketat mungkin sesuai format data yang diharapkan.',
    '<strong>Encode data on output.</strong> At the point where user-controllable data is output in HTTP responses, encode the output to prevent it from being interpreted as active content. Depending on the output context, this might require applying combinations of HTML, URL, JavaScript, and CSS encoding.' => '<strong>Encode data saat output.</strong> Sebelum menulis data ke respons HTTP, terapkan encoding sesuai konteks (HTML, URL, JavaScript, atau CSS) agar browser tidak menafsirkan data sebagai kode aktif.',
    '<strong>Use appropriate response headers.</strong> To prevent XSS in HTTP responses that aren\'t intended to contain any HTML or JavaScript, you can use the [[C0]] and [[C1]] headers to ensure that browsers interpret the responses in the way you intend.' => '<strong>Gunakan header respons yang tepat.</strong> Pada endpoint non-HTML seperti JSON atau file teks, pasang header [[C0]] dan [[C1]] agar browser tidak menafsirkannya sebagai dokumen HTML atau skrip.',
    '<strong>Content Security Policy.</strong> As a last line of defense, you can use Content Security Policy (CSP) to reduce the severity of any XSS vulnerabilities that still occur.' => '<strong>Content Security Policy (CSP).</strong> Sebagai lapisan pertahanan tambahan, terapkan CSP untuk mempersempit dampak celah XSS apabila masih lolos.',
    'How to prevent XSS' => 'Cara mencegah XSS',
    'Find XSS vulnerabilities using Burp Suite\'s web vulnerability scanner' => 'Menemukan kerentanan XSS dengan pemindai kerentanan web',
    'Common questions about cross-site scripting' => 'Pertanyaan umum mengenai cross-site scripting',
    '<strong>How common are XSS vulnerabilities?</strong> XSS vulnerabilities are very common, and XSS is probably the most frequently occurring web security vulnerability.' => '<strong>Seberapa umum celah XSS?</strong> Sangat umum, bahkan menjadi salah satu kerentanan aplikasi web yang paling sering ditemukan.',
    '<strong>How common are XSS attacks?</strong> It is difficult to get reliable data about real-world XSS attacks, but it is probably less frequently exploited than other vulnerabilities.' => '<strong>Seberapa sering serangan XSS terjadi?</strong> Statistik insiden nyata bervariasi karena banyak kasus tidak dipublikasikan, namun dampaknya tinggi ketika menyasar akun istimewa.',
    '<strong>What is the difference between XSS and CSRF?</strong> XSS involves causing a web site to return malicious JavaScript, while CSRF involves inducing a victim user to perform actions they do not intend to do.' => '<strong>Apa beda XSS dan CSRF?</strong> XSS membuat situs menjalankan JavaScript berbahaya di browser korban, sedangkan CSRF memaksa browser korban mengirim aksi tidak diinginkan ke situs target.',
    '<strong>What is the difference between XSS and SQL injection?</strong> XSS is a client-side vulnerability that targets other application users, while SQL injection is a server-side vulnerability that targets the application\'s database.' => '<strong>Apa beda XSS dan SQL injection?</strong> XSS menyerang sisi klien (pengguna lain melalui browser), sedangkan SQL injection menyerang sisi server pada lapisan database aplikasi.',
    '<strong>How do I prevent XSS in PHP?</strong> Filter your inputs with a whitelist of allowed characters and use type hints or type casting. Escape your outputs with [[C0]] and [[C1]] for HTML contexts, or JavaScript Unicode escapes for JavaScript contexts.' => '<strong>Bagaimana mencegah XSS di PHP?</strong> Validasi input berbasis daftar izin dan type casting, lalu lakukan escaping output menggunakan [[C0]] dengan [[C1]] pada konteks HTML serta Unicode escaping untuk konteks JavaScript.',
    '<strong>How do I prevent XSS in Java?</strong> Filter your inputs with a whitelist of allowed characters and use a library such as Google Guava to HTML-encode your output for HTML contexts, or use JavaScript Unicode escapes for JavaScript contexts.' => '<strong>Bagaimana mencegah XSS di Java?</strong> Saring input memakai whitelist dan gunakan pustaka encoding tepercaya (seperti OWASP Java Encoder atau Guava) sesuai konteks output HTML maupun JavaScript.',

    // reflected
    'In this section, we\'ll explain reflected cross-site scripting, describe the impact of reflected XSS attacks, and spell out how to find reflected XSS vulnerabilities.' => 'Bagian ini membahas cara kerja reflected cross-site scripting, dampaknya, dan langkah-langkah pengujiannya.',
    'What is reflected cross-site scripting?' => 'Apa itu reflected cross-site scripting?',
    'Reflected cross-site scripting (or XSS) arises when an application receives data in an HTTP request and includes that data within the immediate response in an unsafe way.' => 'Reflected XSS terjadi ketika aplikasi menerima input dari permintaan HTTP lalu langsung mengembalikannya dalam respons saat itu juga tanpa pengamanan.',
    'Suppose a website has a search function which receives the user-supplied search term in a URL parameter:' => 'Misalkan sebuah situs memiliki fitur pencarian yang menerima kata kunci lewat parameter URL:',
    'The application echoes the supplied search term in the response to this URL:' => 'Aplikasi menampilkan kembali kata kunci tersebut ke dalam respons halaman:',
    'Assuming the application doesn\'t perform any other processing of the data, an attacker can construct an attack like this:' => 'Jika tidak ada sanitasi maupun encoding, penyerang dapat menyusun tautan berbahaya seperti berikut:',
    'This URL results in the following response:' => 'URL tersebut menghasilkan respons HTML berikut:',
    'If another user of the application requests the attacker\'s URL, then the script supplied by the attacker will execute in the victim user\'s browser, in the context of their session with the application.' => 'Saat pengguna lain membuka URL milik penyerang, skrip sisipan langsung tereksekusi di browser korban dalam konteks sesinya.',
    'Impact of reflected XSS attacks' => 'Dampak serangan reflected XSS',
    'If an attacker can control a script that is executed in the victim\'s browser, then they can typically fully compromise that user. Amongst other things, the attacker can:' => 'Apabila penyerang mengendalikan skrip yang berjalan di browser korban, akun korban umumnya bisa dikuasai penuh. Penyerang dapat:',
    'Perform any action within the application that the user can perform.' => 'Melakukan tindakan apa pun di aplikasi yang bisa dilakukan korban.',
    'View any information that the user is able to view.' => 'Melihat seluruh informasi yang dapat diakses korban.',
    'Modify any information that the user is able to modify.' => 'Mengubah data yang dapat dimodifikasi oleh korban.',
    'Initiate interactions with other application users, including malicious attacks, that will appear to originate from the initial victim user.' => 'Memulai interaksi atau serangan ke pengguna lain seolah berasal dari akun korban.',
    'There are various means by which an attacker might induce a victim user to make a request that they control, to deliver a reflected XSS attack. These include placing links on a website controlled by the attacker, or on another website that allows content to be generated, or by sending a link in an email, tweet or other message. The attack could be targeted directly against a known user, or could be an indiscriminate attack against any users of the application.' => 'Penyerang memancing korban untuk membuka tautan berbahaya lewat situs pihak ketiga, kolom komentar publik, email, atau pesan singkat, baik secara terarah ke target tertentu maupun secara acak.',
    'The need for an external delivery mechanism for the attack means that the impact of reflected XSS is generally less severe than stored XSS, where a self-contained attack can be delivered within the vulnerable application itself.' => 'Karena membutuhkan pemicu pengiriman tautan dari luar, reflected XSS umumnya dinilai sedikit lebih ringan dibanding stored XSS yang payloadnya tersimpan langsung di dalam aplikasi.',
    'Reflected XSS in different contexts' => 'Reflected XSS di berbagai konteks',
    'There are many different varieties of reflected cross-site scripting. The location of the reflected data within the application\'s response determines what type of payload is required to exploit it and might also affect the impact of the vulnerability.' => 'Ada beragam variasi reflected XSS bergantung pada posisi data yang dipantulkan di respons HTTP, yang menentukan jenis payload dan potensi dampaknya.',
    'In addition, if the application performs any validation or other processing on the submitted data before it is reflected, this will generally affect what kind of XSS payload is needed.' => 'Selain itu, penyaringan atau transformasi data oleh aplikasi sebelum dipantulkan ikut memengaruhi bentuk payload yang diperlukan.',
    'How to find and test for reflected XSS vulnerabilities' => 'Cara menemukan dan menguji kerentanan reflected XSS',
    'The vast majority of reflected cross-site scripting vulnerabilities can be found quickly and reliably using Burp Suite\'s web vulnerability scanner.' => 'Mayoritas kerentanan reflected XSS dapat dideteksi dengan cepat memakai pemindai kerentanan web.',
    'Testing for reflected XSS vulnerabilities manually involves the following steps:' => 'Pengujian manual kerentanan reflected XSS dilakukan lewat tahapan berikut:',
    '<strong>Test every entry point.</strong> Test separately every entry point for data within the application\'s HTTP requests. This includes parameters or other data within the URL query string and message body, and the URL file path. It also includes HTTP headers, although XSS-like behavior that can only be triggered via certain HTTP headers may not be exploitable in practice.' => '<strong>Uji setiap titik input.</strong> Periksa seluruh parameter query string, body permintaan, path URL, hingga header HTTP secara terpisah.',
    '<strong>Submit random alphanumeric values.</strong> For each entry point, submit a unique random value and determine whether the value is reflected in the response. The value should be designed to survive most input validation, so needs to be fairly short and contain only alphanumeric characters. But it needs to be long enough to make accidental matches within the response highly unlikely. A random alphanumeric value of around 8 characters is normally ideal. You can use Burp Intruder\'s [[A0]]number payloads[[/A0]] with randomly generated hex values to generate suitable random values. And you can use Burp Intruder\'s [[A1]]grep payloads settings[[/A1]] to automatically flag responses that contain the submitted value.' => '<strong>Kirim nilai alfanumerik acak.</strong> Masukkan string acak unik sekitar 8 karakter ke tiap titik input agar lolos filter dasar sekaligus terhindar dari kecocokan tak sengaja, lalu periksa bagian mana dari respons yang memantulkan nilai tersebut.',
    '<strong>Determine the reflection context.</strong> For each location within the response where the random value is reflected, determine its context. This might be in text between HTML tags, within a tag attribute which might be quoted, within a JavaScript string, etc.' => '<strong>Tentukan konteks refleksi.</strong> Identifikasi posisi kemunculan nilai di respons, apakah di antara tag HTML, di dalam atribut bertanda kutip, atau di dalam literal string JavaScript.',
    '<strong>Test a candidate payload.</strong> Based on the context of the reflection, test an initial candidate XSS payload that will trigger JavaScript execution if it is reflected unmodified within the response. The easiest way to test payloads is to send the request to [[A0]]Burp Repeater[[/A0]], modify the request to insert the candidate payload, issue the request, and then review the response to see if the payload worked. An efficient way to work is to leave the original random value in the request and place the candidate XSS payload before or after it. Then set the random value as the search term in Burp Repeater\'s response view. Burp will highlight each location where the search term appears, letting you quickly locate the reflection.' => '<strong>Uji payload kandidat.</strong> Berdasarkan konteksnya, kirim payload awal lewat alat pengulang permintaan dan amati apakah karakter sintaks keluar utuh tanpa di-encode.',
    '<strong>Test alternative payloads.</strong> If the candidate XSS payload was modified by the application, or blocked altogether, then you will need to test alternative payloads and techniques that might deliver a working XSS attack based on the context of the reflection and the type of input validation that is being performed. For more details, see [[A0]]cross-site scripting contexts[[/A0]]' => '<strong>Coba payload alternatif.</strong> Bila payload awal disaring atau diblokir, uji variasi payload lain sesuai filter yang aktif dan [[A0]]konteks XSS[[/A0]] yang dihadapi.',
    '<strong>Test the attack in a browser.</strong> Finally, if you succeed in finding a payload that appears to work within Burp Repeater, transfer the attack to a real browser (by pasting the URL into the address bar, or by modifying the request in [[A0]]Burp Proxy\'s intercept view[[/A0]], and see if the injected JavaScript is indeed executed. Often, it is best to execute some simple JavaScript like [[C0]] which will trigger a visible popup within the browser if the attack succeeds.' => '<strong>Verifikasi di browser nyata.</strong> Buka URL atau respons yang telah dimodifikasi di browser sungguhan dengan payload sederhana seperti [[C0]] untuk memastikan JavaScript benar-benar tereksekusi.',
    'Common questions about reflected cross-site scripting' => 'Pertanyaan umum seputar reflected XSS',
    '<strong>What is the difference between reflected XSS and stored XSS?</strong> Reflected XSS arises when an application takes some input from an HTTP request and embeds that input into the immediate response in an unsafe way. With stored XSS, the application instead stores the input and embeds it into a later response in an unsafe way.' => '<strong>Apa beda reflected XSS dan stored XSS?</strong> Pada reflected XSS, input langsung dipantulkan ke respons saat itu juga. Pada stored XSS, input disimpan terlebih dahulu di server lalu disajikan pada respons berikutnya.',
    '<strong>What is the difference between reflected XSS and self-XSS?</strong> Self-XSS involves similar application behavior to regular reflected XSS, however it cannot be triggered in normal ways via a crafted URL or a cross-domain request. Instead, the vulnerability is only triggered if the victim themselves submits the XSS payload from their browser. Delivering a self-XSS attack normally involves socially engineering the victim to paste some attacker-supplied input into their browser. As such, it is normally considered to be a lame, low-impact issue.' => '<strong>Apa beda reflected XSS dan self-XSS?</strong> Self-XSS tidak dapat dipicu lewat tautan eksternal atau permintaan lintas domain, melainkan menuntut korban mengetik atau menempelkan payload sendiri di browsernya lewat rekayasa sosial, sehingga dampaknya umumnya rendah.',

    // stored
    'In this section, we\'ll explain stored cross-site scripting, describe the impact of stored XSS attacks, and spell out how to find stored XSS vulnerabilities.' => 'Bagian ini menjelaskan stored cross-site scripting, dampaknya, dan strategi mencari celah stored XSS secara sistematis.',
    'What is stored cross-site scripting?' => 'Apa itu stored cross-site scripting?',
    'Stored cross-site scripting (also known as second-order or persistent XSS) arises when an application receives data from an untrusted source and includes that data within its later HTTP responses in an unsafe way.' => 'Stored cross-site scripting (atau second-order / persistent XSS) terjadi ketika aplikasi menyimpan data dari sumber tidak tepercaya lalu menyertakannya pada respons HTTP berikutnya tanpa pengamanan.',
    'Suppose a website allows users to submit comments on blog posts, which are displayed to other users. Users submit comments using an HTTP request like the following:' => 'Misalkan sebuah blog membolehkan pengguna mengirim komentar yang ditampilkan kepada pengunjung lain melalui permintaan HTTP berikut:',
    'After this comment has been submitted, any user who visits the blog post will receive the following within the application\'s response:' => 'Setelah komentar tersimpan, setiap pengunjung blog akan menerima HTML berikut di responsnya:',
    'Assuming the application doesn\'t perform any other processing of the data, an attacker can submit a malicious comment like this:' => 'Jika input tidak divalidasi atau di-encode, penyerang dapat mengirim komentar berisi payload berbahaya:',
    'Within the attacker\'s request, this comment would be URL-encoded as:' => 'Di dalam permintaan HTTP, komentar itu dikirim dalam bentuk URL-encoded seperti berikut:',
    'Any user who visits the blog post will now receive the following within the application\'s response:' => 'Pengunjung mana pun yang membuka artikel blog tersebut akan menerima markup berikut:',
    'The script supplied by the attacker will then execute in the victim user\'s browser, in the context of their session with the application.' => 'Skrip sisipan otomatis berjalan di browser korban dalam konteks sesi login masing-masing pengunjung.',
    'Impact of stored XSS attacks' => 'Dampak serangan stored XSS',
    'If an attacker can control a script that is executed in the victim\'s browser, then they can typically fully compromise that user. The attacker can carry out any of the actions that are applicable to the impact of [[A0]]reflected XSS vulnerabilities[[/A0]].' => 'Ketika skrip penyerang berjalan di browser korban, dampak utamanya setara dengan [[A0]]reflected XSS[[/A0]], yaitu pengambilalihan penuh akun dan aksi korban.',
    'In terms of exploitability, the key difference between reflected and stored XSS is that a stored XSS vulnerability enables attacks that are self-contained within the application itself. The attacker does not need to find an external way of inducing other users to make a particular request containing their exploit. Rather, the attacker places their exploit into the application itself and simply waits for users to encounter it.' => 'Dari sisi eksploitasi, keunggulan stored XSS adalah sifatnya yang mandiri di dalam aplikasi. Penyerang tidak perlu membujuk korban mengklik tautan eksternal; cukup tanam payload sekali lalu tunggu korban membuka halaman terkait.',
    'The self-contained nature of stored cross-site scripting exploits is particularly relevant in situations where an XSS vulnerability only affects users who are currently logged in to the application. If the XSS is reflected, then the attack must be fortuitously timed: a user who is induced to make the attacker\'s request at a time when they are not logged in will not be compromised. In contrast, if the XSS is stored, then the user is guaranteed to be logged in at the time they encounter the exploit.' => 'Karakteristik ini sangat penting saat celah hanya berdampak pada pengguna yang sedang login. Pada reflected XSS, korban bisa saja belum login saat mengklik link, sedangkan pada stored XSS payload otomatis tereksekusi tepat saat pengguna aktif membuka halaman tersebut.',
    'Stored XSS in different contexts' => 'Stored XSS di berbagai konteks',
    'There are many different varieties of stored cross-site scripting. The location of the stored data within the application\'s response determines what type of payload is required to exploit it and might also affect the impact of the vulnerability.' => 'Seperti reflected XSS, posisi data tersimpan di halaman respons menentukan konteks HTML/JS serta jenis payload yang dibutuhkan.',
    'In addition, if the application performs any validation or other processing on the data before it is stored, or at the point when the stored data is incorporated into responses, this will generally affect what kind of XSS payload is needed.' => 'Validasi yang diterapkan saat penyimpanan maupun saat pembacaan ulang juga sangat menentukan bentuk payload yang dapat lolos.',
    'How to find and test for stored XSS vulnerabilities' => 'Cara menemukan dan menguji kerentanan stored XSS',
    'Many stored XSS vulnerabilities can be found using Burp Suite\'s web vulnerability scanner.' => 'Banyak kerentanan stored XSS dapat ditemukan lewat pemindai kerentanan web.',
    'Testing for stored XSS vulnerabilities manually can be challenging. You need to test all relevant "entry points" via which attacker-controllable data can enter the application\'s processing, and all "exit points" at which that data might appear in the application\'s responses.' => 'Pengujian stored XSS secara manual menuntut penelusuran menyeluruh terhadap seluruh titik masuk data (entry point) sekaligus seluruh titik kemunculannya (exit point) di berbagai halaman.',
    'Entry points into the application\'s processing include:' => 'Titik masuk data ke pemrosesan aplikasi mencakup:',
    'Parameters or other data within the URL query string and message body.' => 'Parameter query string maupun body permintaan HTTP.',
    'The URL file path.' => 'Path URL.',
    'HTTP request headers that might not be exploitable in relation to reflected XSS.' => 'Header permintaan HTTP (yang mungkin tidak langsung tereksploitasi di skenario reflected).',
    'Any out-of-band routes via which an attacker can deliver data into the application. The routes that exist depend entirely on the functionality implemented by the application: a webmail application will process data received in emails; an application displaying a Twitter feed might process data contained in third-party tweets; and a news aggregator will include data originating on other web sites.' => 'Kanal luar jalur seperti isi email pada aplikasi webmail, feed media sosial pihak ketiga, atau agregator berita yang menarik konten situs eksternal.',
    'The exit points for stored XSS attacks are all possible HTTP responses that are returned to any kind of application user in any situation.' => 'Adapun titik keluarnya meliputi semua halaman respons HTTP yang dilihat peran pengguna mana pun, termasuk halaman admin.',
    'The first step in testing for stored XSS vulnerabilities is to locate the links between entry and exit points, whereby data submitted to an entry point is emitted from an exit point. The reasons why this can be challenging are that:' => 'Langkah pertama adalah memetakan keterkaitan antara titik masuk dan titik keluar. Tantangan utamanya meliputi:',
    'Data submitted to any entry point could in principle be emitted from any exit point. For example, user-supplied display names could appear within an obscure audit log that is only visible to some application users.' => 'Data dari satu titik masuk bisa saja muncul di halaman tersembunyi seperti log audit yang hanya dilihat admin.',
    'Data that is currently stored by the application is often vulnerable to being overwritten due to other actions performed within the application. For example, a search function might display a list of recent searches, which are quickly replaced as users perform other searches.' => 'Data tersimpan sering cepat tertimpa oleh aktivitas lain, misalnya daftar riwayat pencarian terbaru.',
    'To comprehensively identify links between entry and exit points would involve testing each permutation separately, submitting a specific value into the entry point, navigating directly to the exit point, and determining whether the value appears there. However, this approach is not practical in an application with more than a few pages.' => 'Menguji setiap kombinasi satu per satu sering tidak praktis pada aplikasi besar dengan puluhan halaman.',
    'Instead, a more realistic approach is to work systematically through the data entry points, submitting a specific value into each one, and monitoring the application\'s responses to detect cases where the submitted value appears. Particular attention can be paid to relevant application functions, such as comments on blog posts. When the submitted value is observed in a response, you need to determine whether the data is indeed being stored across different requests, as opposed to being simply reflected in the immediate response.' => 'Pendekatan yang lebih realistis adalah mengirim nilai pelacak unik secara sistematis di tiap titik masuk sambil memantau kemunculannya saat menjelajahi berbagai fitur aplikasi, terutama kolom komentar atau profil, lalu memastikan data benar-benar tersimpan lintas permintaan.',
    'When you have identified links between entry and exit points in the application\'s processing, each link needs to be specifically tested to detect if a stored XSS vulnerability is present. This involves determining the context within the response where the stored data appears and testing suitable candidate XSS payloads that are applicable to that context. At this point, the testing methodology is broadly the same as for finding [[A0]]reflected XSS vulnerabilities[[/A0]].' => 'Setelah jalur titik masuk ke titik keluar ditemukan, tiap jalur diuji konteks output dan payload-nya memakai metodologi yang sama seperti pengujian [[A0]]reflected XSS[[/A0]].',

    // dom-based xss
    'In this section, we\'ll describe DOM-based cross-site scripting (DOM XSS), explain how to find DOM XSS vulnerabilities, and talk about how to exploit DOM XSS with different sources and sinks.' => 'Bagian ini menjelaskan cara kerja DOM-based cross-site scripting (DOM XSS), metode pengujiannya, serta teknik eksploitasinya pada berbagai source dan sink.',
    'What is DOM-based cross-site scripting?' => 'Apa itu DOM-based cross-site scripting?',
    'DOM-based XSS vulnerabilities usually arise when JavaScript takes data from an attacker-controllable source, such as the URL, and passes it to a sink that supports dynamic code execution, such as [[C0]] or [[C1]]. This enables attackers to execute malicious JavaScript, which typically allows them to hijack other users\' accounts.' => 'DOM-based XSS muncul ketika JavaScript membaca data dari sumber yang bisa dikendalikan penyerang (seperti URL) lalu meneruskannya ke sink yang mengeksekusi kode dinamis atau menulis HTML seperti [[C0]] maupun [[C1]].',
    'To deliver a DOM-based XSS attack, you need to place data into a source so that it is propagated to a sink and causes execution of arbitrary JavaScript.' => 'Untuk melancarkan DOM XSS, data berbahaya ditempatkan ke sebuah source agar mengalir ke sink dan mengeksekusi JavaScript sembarang.',
    'The most common source for DOM XSS is the URL, which is typically accessed with the [[C0]] object. An attacker can construct a link to send a victim to a vulnerable page with a payload in the query string and fragment portions of the URL. In certain circumstances, such as when targeting a 404 page or a website running PHP, the payload can also be placed in the path.' => 'Source paling umum adalah URL yang diakses melalui [[C0]]. Payload bisa ditaruh di query string, fragment hash, atau bahkan path URL (misalnya pada halaman 404 atau rute PHP tertentu).',
    'For a detailed explanation of the taint flow between sources and sinks, please refer to the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page.' => 'Untuk memahami konsep aliran data source ke sink secara lebih mendalam, pelajari halaman [[A0]]kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]].',
    'How to test for DOM-based cross-site scripting' => 'Cara menguji DOM-based cross-site scripting',
    'The majority of DOM XSS vulnerabilities can be found quickly and reliably using Burp Suite\'s web vulnerability scanner. To test for DOM-based cross-site scripting manually, you generally need to use a browser with developer tools, such as Chrome. You need to work through each available source in turn, and test each one individually.' => 'Pengujian manual DOM XSS memerlukan browser dengan Developer Tools (seperti DevTools Chrome) untuk menelusuri tiap source secara bergiliran hingga mencapai sink.',
    'Testing HTML sinks' => 'Menguji sink HTML',
    'To test for DOM XSS in an HTML sink, place a random alphanumeric string into the source (such as [[C0]]), then use developer tools to inspect the HTML and find where your string appears. Note that the browser\'s "View source" option won\'t work for DOM XSS testing because it doesn\'t take account of changes that have been performed in the HTML by JavaScript. In Chrome\'s developer tools, you can use [[C1]] (or [[C2]] on MacOS) to search the DOM for your string.' => 'Masukkan string alfanumerik acak ke source (seperti [[C0]]) lalu cari kemunculannya di panel Elements pada DevTools (tekan [[C1]] atau [[C2]] di macOS). Menu View Source biasa tidak menunjukkan hasil perubahan DOM oleh JavaScript.',
    'For each location where your string appears within the DOM, you need to identify the context. Based on this context, you need to refine your input to see how it is processed. For example, if your string appears within a double-quoted attribute then try to inject double quotes in your string to see if you can break out of the attribute.' => 'Di setiap lokasi kemunculan pada DOM, identifikasi konteksnya lalu uji apakah karakter pemecah konteks seperti tanda kutip atau kurung sudut lolos tanpa di-encode.',
    'Note that browsers behave differently with regards to URL-encoding, Chrome, Firefox, and Safari will URL-encode [[C0]] and [[C1]], while IE11 and Microsoft Edge (pre-Chromium) will not URL-encode these sources. If your data gets URL-encoded before being processed, then an XSS attack is unlikely to work.' => 'Perlu dicatat bahwa Chrome, Firefox, dan Safari otomatis melakukan URL-encoding pada [[C0]] serta [[C1]], sedangkan browser lama tidak. Bila nilai sudah ter-URL-encode sebelum masuk sink, payload HTML sering kali gagal dieksekusi kecuali didekode terlebih dahulu oleh aplikasi.',
    'Testing JavaScript execution sinks' => 'Menguji sink eksekusi JavaScript',
    'Testing JavaScript execution sinks for DOM-based XSS is a little harder. With these sinks, your input doesn\'t necessarily appear anywhere within the DOM, so you can\'t search for it. Instead you\'ll need to use the JavaScript debugger to determine whether and how your input is sent to a sink.' => 'Sink eksekusi JavaScript lebih menantang karena input tidak selalu muncul di pohon DOM. Anda perlu memakai debugger JavaScript untuk melacak aliran variabel hingga mencapai sink.',
    'For each potential source, such as [[C0]], you first need to find cases within the page\'s JavaScript code where the source is being referenced. In Chrome\'s developer tools, you can use [[C1]] (or [[C2]] on MacOS) to search all the page\'s JavaScript code for the source.' => 'Cari semua referensi ke source seperti [[C0]] di seluruh berkas JavaScript menggunakan pencarian global DevTools ([[C1]] atau [[C2]]).',
    'Once you\'ve found where the source is being read, you can use the JavaScript debugger to add a break point and follow how the source\'s value is used. You might find that the source gets assigned to other variables. If this is the case, you\'ll need to use the search function again to track these variables and see if they\'re passed to a sink. When you find a sink that is being assigned data that originated from the source, you can use the debugger to inspect the value by hovering over the variable to show its value before it is sent to the sink. Then, as with HTML sinks, you need to refine your input to see if you can deliver a successful XSS attack.' => 'Pasang breakpoint pada titik pembacaan source untuk mengikuti alurnya melewati variabel perantara hingga tiba di sink, lalu periksa nilai variabelnya dan sesuaikan payload agar eksekusi JavaScript berhasil.',
    'Testing for DOM XSS using DOM Invader' => 'Menguji DOM XSS memakai DOM Invader',
    'Identifying and exploiting DOM XSS in the wild can be a tedious process, often requiring you to manually trawl through complex, minified JavaScript. If you use Burp\'s browser, however, you can take advantage of its built-in DOM Invader extension, which does a lot of the hard work for you.' => 'Menelusuri JavaScript ter-minify secara manual bisa memakan waktu. Ekstensi seperti DOM Invader menginstrumentasi sumber dan sink browser untuk menyoroti aliran taint secara otomatis.',
    'DOM Invader documentation' => 'Dokumentasi DOM Invader',
    'Exploiting DOM XSS with different sources and sinks' => 'Mengeksploitasi DOM XSS pada berbagai source dan sink',
    'In principle, a website is vulnerable to DOM-based cross-site scripting if there is an executable path via which data can propagate from source to sink. In practice, different sources and sinks have differing properties and behavior that can affect exploitability, and determine what techniques are necessary. Additionally, the website\'s scripts might perform validation or other processing of data that must be accommodated when attempting to exploit a vulnerability. There are a variety of sinks that are relevant to DOM-based vulnerabilities. Please refer to the [[A0]]list[[/A0]] below for details.' => 'Secara prinsip, DOM XSS terjadi bila ada jalur eksekusi dari source menuju sink. Dalam praktiknya, sifat tiap source dan sink serta proses validasi di antara keduanya menentukan bentuk payload yang berhasil. Lihat [[A0]]daftar sink[[/A0]] di bawah untuk rincian.',
    'The [[C0]] sink works with [[C1]] elements, so you can use a simple payload, such as the one below:' => 'Sink [[C0]] mendukung elemen [[C1]], sehingga payload sederhana berikut dapat langsung berjalan:',
    'Note, however, that in some situations the content that is written to [[C0]] includes some surrounding context that you need to take account of in your exploit. For example, you might need to close some existing elements before using your JavaScript payload.' => 'Namun perhatikan elemen HTML di sekitarnya saat menulis ke [[C0]]; terkadang Anda perlu menutup tag atau atribut yang sedang terbuka lebih dulu.',
    'The [[C0]] sink doesn\'t accept [[C1]] elements on any modern browser, nor will [[C2]] events fire. This means you will need to use alternative elements like [[C3]] or [[C4]]. Event handlers such as [[C5]] and [[C6]] can be used in conjunction with these elements. For example:' => 'Sink [[C0]] di browser modern tidak mengeksekusi tag [[C1]] baru maupun event [[C2]], sehingga Anda perlu memakai elemen seperti [[C3]] atau [[C4]] disertai event handler [[C5]] atau [[C6]], misalnya:',
    'Sources and sinks in third-party dependencies' => 'Source dan sink pada pustaka pihak ketiga',
    'Modern web applications are typically built using a number of third-party libraries and frameworks, which often provide additional functions and capabilities for developers. It\'s important to remember that some of these are also potential sources and sinks for DOM XSS.' => 'Aplikasi modern bergantung pada berbagai pustaka dan framework pihak ketiga, dan fungsi utilitas di dalamnya juga dapat menjadi source atau sink untuk DOM XSS.',
    'DOM XSS in jQuery' => 'DOM XSS di jQuery',
    'If a JavaScript library such as jQuery is being used, look out for sinks that can alter DOM elements on the page. For instance, jQuery\'s [[C0]] function can change the attributes of DOM elements. If data is read from a user-controlled source like the URL, then passed to the [[C1]] function, then it may be possible to manipulate the value sent to cause XSS. For example, here we have some JavaScript that changes an anchor element\'s [[C2]] attribute using data from the URL:' => 'Pada jQuery, perhatikan fungsi yang mengubah elemen atau atribut DOM seperti [[C0]]. Jika input pengguna dari URL diteruskan ke [[C1]] untuk mengisi atribut [[C2]] tautan, penyerang dapat menyuntikkan skema berbahaya:',
    'You can exploit this by modifying the URL so that the [[C0]] source contains a malicious JavaScript URL. After the page\'s JavaScript applies this malicious URL to the back link\'s [[C1]], clicking on the back link will execute it:' => 'Eksploitasi dilakukan dengan menyisipkan skema pseudo-URL ke parameter [[C0]] agar saat tautan diklik, kode JavaScript tereksekusi melalui atribut [[C1]]:',
    'Another potential sink to look out for is jQuery\'s [[C0]] selector function, which can be used to inject malicious objects into the DOM.' => 'Sink jQuery lain yang perlu diawasi adalah fungsi selektor [[C0]] yang dapat menafsirkan string sebagai elemen HTML baru di DOM.',
    'jQuery used to be extremely popular, and a classic DOM XSS vulnerability was caused by websites using this selector in conjunction with the [[C0]] source for animations or auto-scrolling to a particular element on the page. This behavior was often implemented using a vulnerable [[C1]] event handler, similar to the following:' => 'Pola klasik yang sering rentan memakai selektor ini bersama [[C0]] dan event handler [[C1]] untuk menggulir otomatis ke elemen tertentu:',
    'As the [[C0]] is user controllable, an attacker could use this to inject an XSS vector into the [[C1]] selector sink. More recent versions of jQuery have patched this particular vulnerability by preventing you from injecting HTML into a selector when the input begins with a hash character ([[C2]]). However, you may still find vulnerable code in the wild.' => 'Karena [[C0]] dikendalikan pengguna, penyerang dapat memasukkan vektor HTML ke selektor [[C1]]. Versi jQuery baru memblokir penafsiran HTML bila diawali tanda [[C2]], namun versi lama masih banyak ditemukan.',
    'To actually exploit this classic vulnerability, you\'ll need to find a way to trigger a [[C0]] event without user interaction. One of the simplest ways of doing this is to deliver your exploit via an [[C1]]:' => 'Agar event [[C0]] berjalan tanpa klik pengguna, eksploitasi sering dibungkus lewat [[C1]] yang memodifikasi fragment URL setelah dimuat:',
    'In this example, the [[C0]] attribute points to the vulnerable page with an empty hash value. When the [[C1]] is loaded, an XSS vector is appended to the hash, causing the [[C2]] event to fire.' => 'Pada contoh tersebut, [[C0]] memuat halaman target dengan hash kosong lalu segera menambah payload ke hash begitu [[C1]] selesai dimuat, sehingga memicu [[C2]].',
    'Even newer versions of jQuery can still be vulnerable via the [[C0]] selector sink, provided you have full control over its input from a source that doesn\'t require a [[C1]] prefix.' => 'Bahkan versi jQuery terbaru tetap bisa rentan pada sink [[C0]] jika inputnya datang dari sumber yang tidak diawali karakter [[C1]].',
    'DOM XSS in AngularJS' => 'DOM XSS di AngularJS',
    'If a framework like AngularJS is used, it may be possible to execute JavaScript without angle brackets or events. When a site uses the [[C0]] attribute on an HTML element, it will be processed by AngularJS. In this case, AngularJS will execute JavaScript inside double curly braces that can occur directly in HTML or inside attributes.' => 'Jika situs memakai AngularJS dengan atribut [[C0]], ekspresi di dalam kurung kurawal ganda akan dievaluasi oleh AngularJS sehingga JavaScript dapat berjalan tanpa memerlukan tanda kurung sudut atau event HTML.',
    'DOM XSS combined with reflected and stored data' => 'DOM XSS yang digabung dengan data reflected dan stored',
    'Some pure DOM-based vulnerabilities are self-contained within a single page. If a script reads some data from the URL and writes it to a dangerous sink, then the vulnerability is entirely client-side.' => 'Sebagian celah DOM murni terjadi seluruhnya di sisi klien saat skrip membaca URL lalu menulisnya ke sink berbahaya.',
    'However, sources aren\'t limited to data that is directly exposed by browsers - they can also originate from the website. For example, websites often reflect URL parameters in the HTML response from the server. This is commonly associated with normal XSS, but it can also lead to reflected DOM XSS vulnerabilities.' => 'Namun source tidak harus berasal langsung dari browser; data juga bisa dipantulkan atau disimpan oleh server lalu diproses secara tidak aman oleh skrip sisi klien.',
    'In a reflected DOM XSS vulnerability, the server processes data from the request, and echoes the data into the response. The reflected data might be placed into a JavaScript string literal, or a data item within the DOM, such as a form field. A script on the page then processes the reflected data in an unsafe way, ultimately writing it to a dangerous sink.' => 'Pada reflected DOM XSS, server memantulkan input ke respons (misalnya ke dalam data JSON atau atribut form), lalu skrip di halaman mengambil nilai tersebut dan mengirimkannya ke sink berbahaya.',
    'Websites may also store data on the server and reflect it elsewhere. In a stored DOM XSS vulnerability, the server receives data from one request, stores it, and then includes the data in a later response. A script within the later response contains a sink which then processes the data in an unsafe way.' => 'Pada stored DOM XSS, server menyimpan data dari satu permintaan lalu menyertakannya di respons berikutnya untuk diproses oleh sink berbahaya di skrip klien.',
    'Which sinks can lead to DOM-XSS vulnerabilities?' => 'Sink mana saja yang dapat menyebabkan kerentanan DOM-XSS?',
    'The following are some of the main sinks that can lead to DOM-XSS vulnerabilities:' => 'Berikut sejumlah sink utama yang kerap memicu kerentanan DOM-XSS:',
    'The following jQuery functions are also sinks that can lead to DOM-XSS vulnerabilities:' => 'Fungsi-fungsi jQuery berikut juga termasuk sink potensial untuk DOM-XSS:',
    'How to prevent DOM-XSS vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan DOM-XSS',
    'In addition to the general measures described on the [[A0]]DOM-based vulnerabilities[[/A0]] page, you should avoid allowing data from any untrusted source to be dynamically written to the HTML document.' => 'Selain langkah pada halaman [[A0]]kerentanan berbasis DOM[[/A0]], hindari menulis data dari sumber luar secara dinamis ke dokumen HTML.',

    // contexts
    'When testing for [[A0]]reflected[[/A0]] and [[A1]]stored[[/A1]] XSS, a key task is to identify the XSS context:' => 'Saat menguji [[A0]]reflected[[/A0]] maupun [[A1]]stored[[/A1]] XSS, tugas utamanya adalah mengenali konteks kemunculan input:',
    'The location within the response where attacker-controllable data appears.' => 'Lokasi di dalam respons HTML tempat data input muncul.',
    'Any input validation or other processing that is being performed on that data by the application.' => 'Proses validasi, penyaringan, atau transformasi yang dilakukan aplikasi pada data tersebut.',
    'Based on these details, you can then select one or more candidate XSS payloads, and test whether they are effective.' => 'Berdasarkan dua informasi tadi, Anda dapat memilih payload kandidat yang tepat dan menguji keefektifannya.',
    'We have built a comprehensive [[A0]]XSS cheat sheet[[/A0]] to help testing web applications and filters. You can filter by events and tags and see which vectors require user interaction. The cheat sheet also contains AngularJS sandbox escapes and many other sections to help with XSS research.' => 'Tersedia juga [[A0]]contekan XSS[[/A0]] lengkap berisi daftar tag, event, dan vektor bypass filter untuk referensi pengujian.',
    'XSS between HTML tags' => 'XSS di antara tag HTML',
    'When the XSS context is text between HTML tags, you need to introduce some new HTML tags designed to trigger execution of JavaScript.' => 'Jika data berada di teks biasa di antara tag HTML, Anda cukup menyisipkan tag HTML baru yang mengeksekusi JavaScript.',
    'Some useful ways of executing JavaScript are:' => 'Beberapa cara umum untuk mengeksekusi JavaScript pada konteks ini adalah:',
    'XSS in HTML tag attributes' => 'XSS di dalam atribut tag HTML',
    'When the XSS context is into an HTML tag attribute value, you might sometimes be able to terminate the attribute value, close the tag, and introduce a new one. For example:' => 'Jika input masuk ke nilai atribut tag HTML, terkadang Anda dapat menutup tanda kutip atribut, menutup tag tersebut, lalu menyisipkan tag baru:',
    'More commonly in this situation, angle brackets are blocked or encoded, so your input cannot break out of the tag in which it appears. Provided you can terminate the attribute value, you can normally introduce a new attribute that creates a scriptable context, such as an event handler. For example:' => 'Sering kali tanda kurung sudut diblokir atau di-encode sehingga Anda tidak bisa keluar dari tag. Selama tanda kutip atribut bisa ditutup, Anda tetap dapat menyuntikkan atribut event handler baru seperti:',
    'The above payload creates an [[C0]] event that will execute JavaScript when the element receives the focus, and also adds the [[C1]] attribute to try to trigger the [[C2]] event automatically without any user interaction. Finally, it adds [[C3]] to gracefully repair the following markup.' => 'Payload di atas menambahkan event [[C0]] beserta atribut [[C1]] agar event [[C2]] langsung aktif otomatis tanpa klik korban, lalu menyertakan [[C3]] untuk merapikan sisa markup.',
    'Sometimes the XSS context is into a type of HTML tag attribute that itself can create a scriptable context. Here, you can execute JavaScript without needing to terminate the attribute value. For example, if the XSS context is into the [[C0]] attribute of an anchor tag, you can use the [[C1]] pseudo-protocol to execute script. For example:' => 'Terkadang input masuk ke atribut yang memang mendukung eksekusi skrip langsung, seperti [[C0]] pada tag tautan, sehingga cukup memakai skema [[C1]] tanpa harus menutup tanda kutip:',
    'You might encounter websites that encode angle brackets but still allow you to inject attributes. Sometimes, these injections are possible even within tags that don\'t usually fire events automatically, such as a canonical tag. You can exploit this behavior using access keys and user interaction on Chrome. Access keys allow you to provide keyboard shortcuts that reference a specific element. The [[C0]] attribute allows you to define a letter that, when pressed in combination with other keys (these vary across different platforms), will cause events to fire. In the next lab you can experiment with access keys and exploit a canonical tag. [[A0]]You can exploit XSS in hidden input fields using a technique invented by SecDevLab Research[[/A0]].' => 'Bila kurung sudut di-encode dan tag tidak memicu event secara otomatis (misalnya tag canonical atau input tersembunyi), atribut [[C0]] dapat dipakai agar pintasan keyboard memicu event handler. Pelajari teknik lanjutan pada [[A0]]riset XSS pada input tersembunyi[[/A0]].',
    'XSS into JavaScript' => 'XSS di dalam blok JavaScript',
    'When the XSS context is some existing JavaScript within the response, a wide variety of situations can arise, with different techniques necessary to perform a successful exploit.' => 'Saat refleksi berada di dalam kode JavaScript yang sudah ada di halaman, teknik eksploitasinya bervariasi bergantung pada struktur skripnya.',
    'Terminating the existing script' => 'Mengakhiri skrip yang ada',
    'In the simplest case, it is possible to simply close the script tag that is enclosing the existing JavaScript, and introduce some new HTML tags that will trigger execution of JavaScript. For example, if the XSS context is as follows:' => 'Pada kasus sederhana, Anda cukup menutup tag penutup script lalu memasukkan tag HTML berbahaya. Misalnya bila konteksnya seperti berikut:',
    'then you can use the following payload to break out of the existing JavaScript and execute your own:' => 'maka payload berikut langsung keluar dari blok JavaScript lama dan mengeksekusi milik Anda:',
    'The reason this works is that the browser first performs HTML parsing to identify the page elements including blocks of script, and only later performs JavaScript parsing to understand and execute the embedded scripts. The above payload leaves the original script broken, with an unterminated string literal. But that doesn\'t prevent the subsequent script being parsed and executed in the normal way.' => 'Cara ini berhasil karena parser HTML browser berjalan lebih dulu sebelum parser JavaScript. Meski skrip pertama terputus dengan error sintaks, blok HTML atau skrip baru setelahnya tetap diproses normal.',
    'Breaking out of a JavaScript string' => 'Keluar dari string JavaScript',
    'In cases where the XSS context is inside a quoted string literal, it is often possible to break out of the string and execute JavaScript directly. It is essential to repair the script following the XSS context, because any syntax errors there will prevent the whole script from executing.' => 'Jika input masuk ke dalam literal string bertanda kutip, payload harus keluar dari kutip string sekaligus memperbaiki sintaks sisa baris agar blok JavaScript tetap valid dan dapat dijalankan.',
    'Some useful ways of breaking out of a string literal are:' => 'Beberapa payload umum untuk keluar dari string JavaScript antara lain:',
    'Some applications attempt to prevent input from breaking out of the JavaScript string by escaping any single quote characters with a backslash. A backslash before a character tells the JavaScript parser that the character should be interpreted literally, and not as a special character such as a string terminator. In this situation, applications often make the mistake of failing to escape the backslash character itself. This means that an attacker can use their own backslash character to neutralize the backslash that is added by the application.' => 'Sebagian aplikasi mencoba menggagalkan pemecahan string dengan menambahkan backslash sebelum tanda kutip. Namun bila karakter backslash itu sendiri lupa di-escape, penyerang bisa mengirim backslash sendiri untuk menetralkan escape buatan aplikasi.',
    'For example, suppose that the input:' => 'Sebagai contoh, jika input:',
    'gets converted to:' => 'diubah menjadi:',
    'You can now use the alternative payload:' => 'Anda cukup menyisipkan payload alternatif berikut:',
    'which gets converted to:' => 'yang akan diubah menjadi:',
    'Here, the first backslash means that the second backslash is interpreted literally, and not as a special character. This means that the quote is now interpreted as a string terminator, and so the attack succeeds.' => 'Di sini backslash pertama menandai backslash kedua sebagai karakter biasa, sehingga tanda kutip tetap menutup string JavaScript dan serangan berhasil.',
    'Some websites make XSS more difficult by restricting which characters you are allowed to use. This can be on the website level or by deploying a WAF that prevents your requests from ever reaching the website. In these situations, you need to experiment with other ways of calling functions which bypass these security measures. One way of doing this is to use the [[C0]] statement with an exception handler. This enables you to pass arguments to a function without using parentheses. The following code assigns the [[C1]] function to the global exception handler and the [[C2]] statement passes the [[C3]] to the exception handler (in this case [[C4]]). The end result is that the [[C5]] function is called with [[C6]] as an argument.' => 'Jika filter aplikasi atau WAF memblokir karakter tertentu seperti tanda kurung, teknik seperti pernyataan [[C0]] dengan handler pengecualian global dapat mengirim argumen tanpa tanda kurung sehingga [[C1]] tetap terpanggil lewat mekanisme [[C2]] dengan nilai [[C3]].',
    'There are multiple ways of using this technique to call [[A0]]functions without parentheses[[/A0]].' => 'Ada berbagai variasi teknik serupa untuk [[A0]]memanggil fungsi tanpa tanda kurung[[/A0]].',
    'The next lab demonstrates a website that filters certain characters. You\'ll have to use similar techniques to those described above in order to solve it.' => 'Lab berikutnya mensimulasikan filter karakter ketat yang menuntut teknik bypass serupa.',
    'Making use of HTML-encoding' => 'Memanfaatkan HTML-encoding',
    'When the XSS context is some existing JavaScript within a quoted tag attribute, such as an event handler, it is possible to make use of HTML-encoding to work around some input filters.' => 'Ketika konteks JavaScript berada di dalam atribut event handler tag HTML, HTML-encoding dapat dimanfaatkan untuk melewati filter karakter.',
    'When the browser has parsed out the HTML tags and attributes within a response, it will perform HTML-decoding of tag attribute values before they are processed any further. If the server-side application blocks or sanitizes certain characters that are needed for a successful XSS exploit, you can often bypass the input validation by HTML-encoding those characters.' => 'Browser otomatis melakukan HTML-decoding pada nilai atribut sebelum menyerahkannya ke parser JavaScript. Hal ini memungkinkan entitas HTML seperti entitas kutip melewati filter server.',
    'For example, if the XSS context is as follows:' => 'Sebagai contoh, apabila konteks XSS tampak seperti berikut:',
    'and the application blocks or escapes single quote characters, you can use the following payload to break out of the JavaScript string and execute your own script:' => 'lalu tanda kutip tunggal diblokir atau di-escape, kirimkan entitas HTML seperti berikut:',
    'The [[C0]] sequence is an HTML entity representing an apostrophe or single quote. Because the browser HTML-decodes the value of the [[C1]] attribute before the JavaScript is interpreted, the entities are decoded as quotes, which become string delimiters, and so the attack succeeds.' => 'Urutan [[C0]] adalah entitas HTML untuk tanda kutip tunggal. Karena browser mendekode atribut [[C1]] sebelum mengeksekusi JavaScript, karakter kutip kembali terbentuk dan memecah string.',
    'XSS in JavaScript template literals' => 'XSS di dalam JavaScript template literals',
    'JavaScript template literals are string literals that allow embedded JavaScript expressions. The embedded expressions are evaluated and are normally concatenated into the surrounding text. Template literals are encapsulated in backticks instead of normal quotation marks, and embedded expressions are identified using the [[C0]] syntax.' => 'Template literal JavaScript dibungkus tanda backtick dan mengevaluasi ekspresi yang disisipkan lewat sintaks [[C0]].',
    'For example, the following script will print a welcome message that includes the user\'s display name:' => 'Contohnya skrip berikut menampilkan pesan selamat datang bersama nama tampilan pengguna:',
    'When the XSS context is into a JavaScript template literal, there is no need to terminate the literal. Instead, you simply need to use the [[C0]] syntax to embed a JavaScript expression that will be executed when the literal is processed. For example, if the XSS context is as follows:' => 'Jika input langsung berada di dalam template literal, Anda tidak perlu menutup tanda backtick; cukup sisipkan sintaks [[C0]] secara langsung:',
    'then you can use the following payload to execute JavaScript without terminating the template literal:' => 'maka ekspresi berikut langsung mengeksekusi JavaScript di dalam template literal tersebut:',
    'XSS via client-side template injection' => 'XSS lewat client-side template injection',
    'Some websites use a client-side template framework, such as AngularJS, to dynamically render web pages. If they embed user input into these templates in an unsafe manner, an attacker may be able to inject their own malicious template expressions that launch an XSS attack.' => 'Sebagian situs memakai framework template sisi klien seperti AngularJS untuk merender halaman dinamis. Jika input pengguna masuk ke template tanpa pengamanan, penyerang bisa menyuntikkan ekspresi template berbahaya.',

    // client-side-template-injection
    'In this section, we\'ll look at client-side template injection vulnerabilities and how you can exploit them for XSS attacks. This attack technique was pioneered by our research team - read more in [[A0]]XSS without HTML: Client-Side Template Injection with AngularJS[[/A0]]. Although client-side template injection is a generic issue, we\'ll focus on examples from the AngularJS framework as this is the most common. We\'ll describe how you can craft exploits that escape from the AngularJS sandbox, and how you can potentially use AngularJS features to bypass content security policy (CSP).' => 'Bagian ini membahas kerentanan client-side template injection dan cara mengeksploitasinya menjadi XSS (baca juga riset [[A0]]XSS without HTML dengan AngularJS[[/A0]]). Contoh difokuskan pada AngularJS beserta teknik escape sandbox maupun bypass CSP.',
    'What is client-side template injection?' => 'Apa itu client-side template injection?',
    'Client-side template injection vulnerabilities arise when applications using a client-side template framework dynamically embed user input in web pages. When rendering a page, the framework scans it for template expressions and executes any that it encounters. An attacker can exploit this by supplying a malicious template expression that launches a cross-site scripting (XSS) attack.' => 'Client-side template injection muncul ketika framework template di sisi browser memindai halaman HTML yang memuat input pengguna tak tersaring lalu mengevaluasi ekspresi template di dalamnya, memicu eksekusi XSS.',
    'What is the AngularJS sandbox?' => 'Apa itu sandbox AngularJS?',
    'The AngularJS sandbox is a mechanism that prevents access to potentially dangerous objects, such as [[C0]] or [[C1]], in AngularJS template expressions. It also prevents access to potentially dangerous properties, such as [[C2]]. Despite not being considered a security boundary by the AngularJS team, the wider developer community generally thinks otherwise. Although bypassing the sandbox was initially challenging, security researchers have discovered numerous ways of doing so. As a result, it was eventually removed from AngularJS in version 1.6. However, many legacy applications still use older versions of AngularJS and may be vulnerable as a result.' => 'Sandbox AngularJS membatasi akses ke objek sensitif seperti [[C0]], [[C1]], dan properti [[C2]] di dalam ekspresi template. Walau sempat dianggap mekanisme keamanan, berbagai teknik bypass ditemukan hingga fitur sandbox dihapus pada AngularJS versi 1.6, namun aplikasi versi lama masih terpengaruh.',
    'How does the AngularJS sandbox work?' => 'Bagaimana cara kerja sandbox AngularJS?',
    'The sandbox works by parsing an expression, rewriting the JavaScript, and then using various functions to test whether the rewritten code contains any dangerous objects. For example, the [[C0]] function checks whether a given object references itself. This is one way to detect the [[C1]] object, for example. The [[C2]] constructor is detected in roughly the same way, by checking whether the constructor property references itself.' => 'Sandbox mengurai ekspresi template, menulis ulang JavaScript-nya, lalu memeriksa hasil kode lewat fungsi pemeriksa seperti [[C0]] untuk mencegah referensi ke objek [[C1]] atau konstruktor [[C2]].',
    'The [[C0]] function checks each property access of the object and, if it contains dangerous properties such as [[C1]] or [[C2]], the object will be blocked. The [[C3]]function prevents [[C4]], [[C5]], [[C6]], or [[C7]] from being called.' => 'Fungsi [[C0]] memblokir properti terlarang seperti [[C1]] dan [[C2]], sementara [[C3]] mencegah pemanggilan [[C4]], [[C5]], [[C6]], maupun [[C7]].',
    'You can see the sandbox in action for yourself by visiting [[A0]]this fiddle[[/A0]] and setting a breakpoint at line 13275 of the [[C0]] file. The variable [[C1]] contains your rewritten code, so you can look at how AngularJS transforms it.' => 'Anda bisa mengamati transformasi kode sandbox di dalam variabel [[C1]] pada [[C0]] lewat contoh [[A0]]fiddle ini[[/A0]].',
    'How does an AngularJS sandbox escape work?' => 'Bagaimana cara kerja escape sandbox AngularJS?',
    'A sandbox escape involves tricking the sandbox into thinking the malicious expression is benign. The most well-known escape uses the modified [[C0]] function globally within an expression:' => 'Escape sandbox mengecoh pemeriksa agar mengira ekspresi berbahaya sebagai ekspresi biasa. Contoh terkenal adalah menimpa fungsi [[C0]] secara global:',
    'When it was initially discovered, AngularJS did not prevent this modification. The attack works by overwriting the function using the [[C0]] method, which causes the [[C1]] function to return all the characters sent to it, rather than a specific single character. Due to the logic of the [[C2]] function in AngularJS, it compares what it thinks is a single character against multiple characters. As the first character of the longer string are within the range of the compared characters, the [[C3]] function always returns true, as demonstrated by the following example:' => 'Dengan menimpa metode memakai [[C0]], fungsi [[C1]] mengembalikan seluruh string alih-alih satu huruf, sehingga fungsi [[C2]] menerima string panjang berbahaya seolah pengenal biasa (identifier) seperti terlihat pada [[C3]]:',
    'Once the [[C0]] function is fooled, you can inject malicious JavaScript. For example, an expression such as [[C1]] would be allowed because AngularJS treats every character as an identifier. Note that we need to use AngularJS\'s [[C2]] function because overwriting the [[C3]] function will only take effect once the sandboxed code is executed. This technique would then bypass the sandbox and allow arbitrary JavaScript execution. SecDevLab Research [[A0]]broke the AngularJS sandbox comprehensively, multiple times[[/A0]].' => 'Setelah [[C0]] tertipu, ekspresi [[C1]] diperbolehkan lewat [[C2]] karena efek penimpaan [[C3]] baru berlaku ketika kode dijalankan. Teknik ini dibahas mendalam dalam [[A0]]riset pembobolan sandbox AngularJS[[/A0]].',
    'So you\'ve learned how a basic sandbox escape works, but you may encounter sites that are more restrictive with which characters they allow. For example, a site may prevent you from using double or single quotes. In this situation, you need to use functions such as [[C0]] to generate your characters. Although AngularJS prevents access to the [[C1]] constructor within an expression, you can get round this by using the constructor property of a string instead. This obviously requires a string, so to construct an attack like this, you would need to find a way of creating a string without using single or double quotes.' => 'Bila aplikasi memblokir tanda kutip tunggal maupun ganda, Anda dapat membentuk string memakai [[C0]] melalui properti constructor dari string yang dihasilkan tanpa tanda kutip.',
    'In a standard sandbox escape, you would use [[C0]] to execute your JavaScript payload, but in the lab below, the [[C1]] function is undefined. Fortunately, we can use the [[C2]] filter instead. The typical syntax of an [[C3]] filter is as follows:' => 'Jika fungsi [[C0]] atau [[C1]] tidak tersedia pada skenario tertentu, filter bawaan [[C2]] pada AngularJS dapat dipakai untuk mengevaluasi ekspresi lewat sintaks [[C3]]:',
    'Note that the [[C0]] operator has a different meaning than in JavaScript. Normally, this is a bitwise [[C1]] operation, but in AngularJS it indicates a filter operation. In the code above, we are sending the array [[C2]] on the left to the [[C3]] filter on the right. The colon signifies an argument to send to the filter, which in this case is a string. The [[C4]] filter is normally used to sort an object, but it also accepts an expression, which means we can use it to pass a payload.' => 'Di AngularJS, operator [[C0]] bukan operasi bitwise [[C1]], melainkan operator filter. Array [[C2]] dikirim ke filter [[C3]] dengan argumen ekspresi pengurutan yang dapat dimanfaatkan untuk mengeksekusi payload [[C4]].',
    'You should now have all the tools you need to tackle the next lab.' => 'Dengan pemahaman ini, Anda siap menyelesaikan lab berikut.',
    'How does an AngularJS CSP bypass work?' => 'Bagaimana cara kerja bypass CSP di AngularJS?',
    'Content security policy (CSP) bypasses work in a similar way to standard sandbox escapes, but usually involve some HTML injection. When the CSP mode is active in AngularJS, it parses template expressions differently and avoids using the [[C0]] constructor. This means the standard sandbox escape described above will no longer work.' => 'Bypass CSP pada AngularJS mirip dengan sandbox escape namun menghindari penggunaan konstruktor [[C0]] karena mode CSP mengubah cara framework mengurai ekspresi.',
    'Depending on the specific policy, the CSP will block JavaScript events. However, AngularJS defines its own events that can be used instead. When inside an event, AngularJS defines a special [[C0]] object, which simply references the browser event object. You can use this object to perform a CSP bypass. On Chrome, there is a special property on the [[C1]] object called [[C2]]. This property contains an array of objects that causes the event to be executed. The last property is always the [[C3]] object, which we can use to perform a sandbox escape. By passing this array to the [[C4]] filter, we can enumerate the array and use the last element (the [[C5]] object) to execute a global function, such as [[C6]]. The following code demonstrates this:' => 'Meski event JS biasa diblokir CSP, AngularJS memiliki event internalnya sendiri yang menyediakan objek [[C0]] (referensi ke objek [[C1]]). Properti [[C2]] memuat rantai objek hingga [[C3]], yang dapat diteruskan ke filter [[C4]] agar lewat referensi [[C5]] fungsi global [[C6]] terpanggil:',
    'Notice that the [[C0]] function is used, which allows you to convert an object to an array and call a given function (specified in the second argument) on every element of that array. In this case, we are calling the [[C1]] function. We cannot call the function directly because the AngularJS sandbox would parse the code and detect that the [[C2]] object is being used to call a function. Using the [[C3]] function instead effectively hides the [[C4]] object from the sandbox, allowing us to inject malicious code.' => 'Di sini fungsi [[C0]] memanggil [[C1]] untuk setiap elemen array sehingga referensi objek [[C2]] tersembunyi dari pemeriksaan sandbox melalui pemanggilan tidak langsung lewat [[C3]] terhadap [[C4]].',
    'SecDevLab Research [[A0]]created a CSP bypass using AngularJS in 56 characters using this technique[[/A0]].' => 'Teknik ini memungkinkan penyusunan [[A0]]bypass CSP AngularJS hanya dalam 56 karakter[[/A0]].',
    'This next lab employs a length restriction, so the above vector will not work. In order to exploit the lab, you need to think of various ways of hiding the [[C0]] object from the AngularJS sandbox. One way of doing this is to use the [[C1]] function as follows:' => 'Lab berikut menerapkan batas panjang input sehingga vektor di atas perlu dipadatkan. Salah satu cara menyembunyikan objek [[C0]] dalam kode yang ringkas adalah memakai fungsi [[C1]]:',
    '[[C0]] accepts a function as an argument and will call it for each item in the array. This will bypass the sandbox because the reference to the [[C1]] function is being used without explicitly referencing the [[C2]]. To solve the lab, try various ways of executing [[C3]] without triggering AngularJS\'s [[C4]] detection.' => '[[C0]] menerima referensi fungsi [[C1]] sebagai callback tanpa menulis [[C2]] secara eksplisit, sehingga Anda dapat memicu [[C3]] tanpa terdeteksi pemeriksaan [[C4]] pada sandbox.',
    'How to prevent client-side template injection vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan client-side template injection',
    'To prevent client-side template injection vulnerabilities, avoid using untrusted user input to generate templates or expressions. If this is not practical, consider filtering out template expression syntax from user input prior to embedding it within client-side templates.' => 'Cegah celah ini dengan tidak pernah membentuk template maupun ekspresi sisi klien dari input pengguna yang tidak tepercaya, atau saring sintaks pembatas ekspresi template sebelum menyematkan data.',
    'Note that HTML-encoding is not sufficient to prevent client-side template injection attacks, because frameworks perform an HTML-decode of relevant content prior to locating and executing template expressions.' => 'Perlu diingat bahwa HTML-encoding saja belum cukup, karena framework template klien umumnya mendekode entitas HTML sebelum mengevaluasi ekspresi.',

    // CSP
    'In this section, we\'ll explain what content security policy is, and describe how CSP can be used to mitigate against some common attacks.' => 'Bagian ini menjelaskan cara kerja Content Security Policy (CSP) dan bagaimana kebijakan tersebut memitigasi serangan web umum.',
    'What is CSP (content security policy)?' => 'Apa itu CSP (Content Security Policy)?',
    'CSP is a browser security mechanism that aims to mitigate XSS and some other attacks. It works by restricting the resources (such as scripts and images) that a page can load and restricting whether a page can be framed by other pages.' => 'CSP adalah mekanisme keamanan browser untuk meredam XSS dan sejumlah serangan lain dengan membatasi sumber skrip, gambar, serta hak penyematan halaman dalam frame.',
    'To enable CSP, a response needs to include an HTTP response header called [[C0]] with a value containing the policy. The policy itself consists of one or more directives, separated by semicolons.' => 'CSP diaktifkan dengan menyertakan header HTTP respons [[C0]] berisi kumpulan direktif kebijakan yang dipisahkan tanda titik koma.',
    'The following directive will only allow scripts to be loaded from the [[A0]]same origin[[/A0]] as the page itself:' => 'Direktif berikut hanya mengizinkan pemuatan skrip dari [[A0]]origin yang sama[[/A0]] dengan halaman:',
    'The following directive will only allow scripts to be loaded from a specific domain:' => 'Direktif berikut membatasi skrip hanya dari domain eksternal tertentu:',
    'Care should be taken when allowing scripts from external domains. If there is any way for an attacker to control content that is served from the external domain, then they might be able to deliver an attack. For example, content delivery networks (CDNs) that do not use per-customer URLs, such as [[C0]], should not be trusted, because third parties can get content onto their domains.' => 'Berhati-hatilah saat mengizinkan domain eksternal. Jika pihak luar dapat mengunggah skrip atau file JSONP ke CDN publik bersama seperti [[C0]], penyerang tetap bisa mengeksekusi serangan XSS dari domain terpercaya tersebut.',
    'In addition to whitelisting specific domains, content security policy also provides two other ways of specifying trusted resources: nonces and hashes:' => 'Selain daftar domain, CSP juga mendukung dua metode penandaan skrip tepercaya yaitu nonce dan hash:',
    'The CSP directive can specify a nonce (a random value) and the same value must be used in the tag that loads a script. If the values do not match, then the script will not execute. To be effective as a control, the nonce must be securely generated on each page load and not be guessable by an attacker.' => 'Direktif memakai nilai acak sekali pakai (nonce) yang harus persis sama dengan atribut tag skrip dan tidak boleh dapat ditebak serta wajib diganti tiap pemuatan halaman.',
    'The CSP directive can specify a hash of the contents of the trusted script. If the hash of the actual script does not match the value specified in the directive, then the script will not execute. If the content of the script ever changes, then you will of course need to update the hash value that is specified in the directive.' => 'Direktif menentukan hash kriptografis isi skrip yang sah; perubahan satu karakter saja pada skrip akan menggagalkan eksekusi hingga hash di kebijakan ikut diperbarui.',
    'It\'s quite common for a CSP to block resources like [[C0]]. However, many CSPs do allow image requests. This means you can often use [[C1]] elements to make requests to external servers in order to disclose CSRF tokens, for example.' => 'Banyak kebijakan CSP memblokir [[C0]] namun tetap mengizinkan permintaan gambar, sehingga elemen [[C1]] kerap dimanfaatkan untuk membocorkan token atau data lewat URL keluar.',
    'Some browsers, such as Chrome, have built-in dangling markup mitigation that will block requests containing certain characters, such as raw, unencoded new lines or angle brackets.' => 'Beberapa browser seperti Chrome menyertakan mitigasi bawaan terhadap dangling markup dengan memblokir permintaan gambar jika URL-nya memuat baris baru atau tanda kurung sudut mentah.',
    'Some policies are more restrictive and prevent all forms of external requests. However, it\'s still possible to [[A0]]get round these restrictions by eliciting some user interaction[[/A0]]. To bypass this form of policy, you need to inject an HTML element that, when clicked, will store and send everything enclosed by the injected element to an external server.' => 'Ketika semua permintaan otomatis eksternal diblokir CSP ketat, teknik [[A0]]bypass berbasis interaksi pengguna[[/A0]] masih dapat memanfaatkan elemen tautan atau form klik untuk mengirim data yang tertangkap.',
    'The following directive will only allow images to be loaded from the same origin as the page itself:' => 'Direktif berikut membatasi pemuatan gambar hanya dari origin yang sama:',
    'The following directive will only allow images to be loaded from a specific domain:' => 'Direktif berikut hanya mengizinkan gambar dari domain tertentu:',
    'Note that these policies will prevent some dangling markup exploits, because an easy way to capture data with no user interaction is using an [[C0]] tag. However, it will not prevent other exploits, such as those that inject an anchor tag with a dangling [[C1]] attribute.' => 'Kebijakan gambar tersebut memblokir eksfiltrasi otomatis lewat tag [[C0]], namun belum menutup vektor yang memakai tag tautan dengan atribut [[C1]] terbuka.',
    'You may encounter a website that reflects input into the actual policy, most likely in a [[C0]] directive. If the site reflects a parameter that you can control, you can inject a semicolon to add your own CSP directives. Usually, this [[C1]] directive is the final one in the list. This means you will need to overwrite existing directives in order to exploit this vulnerability and bypass the policy.' => 'Bila aplikasi memantulkan input pengguna ke dalam header CSP (sering kali pada direktif [[C0]]), penyerang dapat menyisipkan titik koma untuk menambahkan direktif baru guna melemahkan [[C1]] atau aturan kebijakan sebelumnya.',
    'Normally, it\'s not possible to overwrite an existing [[C0]] directive. However, Chrome recently introduced the [[C1]] directive, which allows you to control [[C2]] elements, but not events. Crucially, this new directive allows you to [[A0]]overwrite existing [[C3]] directives[[/A0]]. Using this knowledge, you should be able to solve the following lab.' => 'Secara umum direktif [[C0]] tidak bisa ditimpa ulang dalam satu header, namun direktif [[C1]] untuk elemen [[C2]] dapat ditambahkan guna [[A0]]menimpa kebijakan [[C3]] yang lebih lama[[/A0]] di Chrome.',
    'The following directive will only allow the page to be framed by other pages from the same origin:' => 'Direktif berikut hanya mengizinkan halaman disematkan dalam frame dari origin yang sama:',
    'The following directive will prevent framing altogether:' => 'Direktif berikut melarang penyematan halaman dalam frame dari mana pun:',
    'Using content security policy to prevent clickjacking is more flexible than using the X-Frame-Options header because you can specify multiple domains and use wildcards. For example:' => 'Pemakaian CSP untuk mencegah clickjacking lebih fleksibel dibanding X-Frame-Options karena mendukung daftar domain dan wildcard, contohnya:',
    'CSP also validates each frame in the parent frame hierarchy, whereas [[C0]] only validates the top-level frame.' => 'Selain itu, CSP memverifikasi seluruh rantai parent frame, sedangkan [[C0]] di banyak browser lama hanya memeriksa frame teratas.',
    'Using CSP to protect against clickjacking attacks is recommended. You can also combine this with the [[C0]] header to provide protection on older browsers that don\'t support CSP, such as Internet Explorer.' => 'Menggunakan CSP disarankan sebagai pertahanan utama clickjacking dan dapat dipadukan dengan header [[C0]] untuk mendukung browser lama.',

    // dangling-markup
    'In this section, we\'ll explain dangling markup injection, how a typical exploit works, and how to prevent dangling markup attacks.' => 'Bagian ini membahas injeksi dangling markup, cara kerjanya saat eksploitasi, serta cara pencegahannya.',
    'What is dangling markup injection?' => 'Apa itu injeksi dangling markup?',
    'Dangling markup injection is a technique for capturing data cross-domain in situations where a full cross-site scripting attack isn\'t possible.' => 'Injeksi dangling markup adalah teknik membaca data halaman lintas domain ketika injeksi JavaScript penuh (XSS) tidak dimungkinkan.',
    'Suppose an application embeds attacker-controllable data into its responses in an unsafe way:' => 'Misalkan aplikasi menulis input pengguna ke respons HTML tanpa menutup atau menyaring karakter atribut:',
    'Suppose also that the application does not filter or escape the [[C0]] or [[C1]] characters. An attacker can use the following syntax to break out of the quoted attribute value and the enclosing tag, and return to an HTML context:' => 'Jika karakter [[C0]] dan [[C1]] tidak di-escape, penyerang dapat menutup atribut serta tag pembungkusnya agar kembali masuk ke konteks HTML bebas:',
    'In this situation, an attacker would naturally attempt to perform XSS. But suppose that a regular XSS attack is not possible, due to input filters, content security policy, or other obstacles. Here, it might still be possible to deliver a dangling markup injection attack using a payload like the following:' => 'Ketika XSS penuh terhadang filter atau CSP, penyerang tetap bisa menyisipkan tag terbuka dengan atribut yang menggantung seperti ini:',
    'This payload creates an [[C0]] tag and defines the start of a [[C1]] attribute containing a URL on the attacker\'s server. Note that the attacker\'s payload doesn\'t close the [[C2]] attribute, which is left "dangling". When a browser parses the response, it will look ahead until it encounters a single quotation mark to terminate the attribute. Everything up until that character will be treated as being part of the URL and will be sent to the attacker\'s server within the URL query string. Any non-alphanumeric characters, including newlines, will be URL-encoded.' => 'Payload tersebut membuka tag [[C0]] dengan atribut [[C1]] yang tidak ditutup. Saat browser mengurai dokumen, seluruh konten HTML sesudahnya hingga tanda kutip tunggal penutup berikutnya akan dianggap sebagai bagian URL lalu dikirim ke server penyerang melalui query string.',
    'The consequence of the attack is that the attacker can capture part of the application\'s response following the injection point, which might contain sensitive data. Depending on the application\'s functionality, this might include CSRF tokens, email messages, or financial data.' => 'Akibatnya, penyerang mampu menangkap isi respons aplikasi tepat setelah titik injeksi, termasuk token CSRF, isi pesan, atau data sensitif pengguna.',
    'Any attribute that makes an external request can be used for dangling markup.' => 'Atribut apa pun yang memicu permintaan eksternal dapat dimanfaatkan dalam teknik dangling markup.',
    'This next lab is difficult to solve because all external requests are blocked. However, there are certain tags that allow you to store data and retrieve it from an external server later. Solving this lab might require user interaction.' => 'Lab berikut menantang karena permintaan otomatis keluar diblokir, sehingga Anda perlu mencari tag interaktif yang dapat menampung lalu mengirimkan data ke server penyerang.',
    'How to prevent dangling markup attacks' => 'Cara mencegah serangan dangling markup',
    'You can prevent dangling markup attacks using the same general defenses for [[A0]]preventing cross-site scripting[[/A0]], by encoding data on output and validating input on arrival.' => 'Cegah serangan dangling markup memakai langkah [[A0]]pencegahan XSS[[/A0]] standar berupa output encoding sesuai konteks dan validasi input yang ketat.',
    'You can also mitigate some dangling markup attacks using [[A0]]content security policy[[/A0]] (CSP). For example, you can prevent some (but not all) attacks, using a policy that prevent tags like [[C0]] from loading external resources.' => 'Dampak sebagian teknik dangling markup juga dapat ditekan lewat [[A0]]Content Security Policy[[/A0]] (CSP), misalnya membatasi sumber gambar tag [[C0]].',
    'The Chrome browser has decided to tackle dangling markup attacks by preventing tags like [[C0]] from defining URLs containing raw characters such as angle brackets and newlines. This will prevent attacks since the data that would otherwise be captured will generally contain those raw characters, so the attack is blocked.' => 'Browser seperti Chrome memitigasi teknik ini pada tag [[C0]] dengan menolak permintaan apabila URL hasil tangkapan mengandung karakter baris baru atau kurung sudut mentah.',

    // exploiting
    'The traditional way to prove that you\'ve found a cross-site scripting vulnerability is to create a popup using the [[C0]] function. This isn\'t because XSS has anything to do with popups; it\'s simply a way to prove that you can execute arbitrary JavaScript on a given domain. You might notice some people using [[C1]]. This is a way of making it explicit which domain the JavaScript is executing on.' => 'Cara klasik membuktikan temuan XSS adalah memunculkan popup memakai [[C0]] atau [[C1]] guna menunjukkan bahwa JavaScript sembarang benar-benar berjalan pada origin domain target.',
    'Sometimes you\'ll want to go further and prove that an XSS vulnerability is a real threat by providing a full exploit. In this section, we\'ll explore three of the most popular and powerful ways to exploit an XSS vulnerability.' => 'Saat membuktikan dampak nyata pada pengujian, penguji sering menyusun skenario eksploitasi penuh. Bagian ini menguraikan tiga skenario eksploitasi XSS yang paling umum dan berdampak besar.',
    'Exploiting cross-site scripting to steal cookies' => 'Mengeksploitasi XSS untuk mencuri cookie',
    'Stealing cookies is a traditional way to exploit XSS. Most web applications use cookies for session handling. You can exploit cross-site scripting vulnerabilities to send the victim\'s cookies to your own domain, then manually inject the cookies into the browser and impersonate the victim.' => 'Mencuri cookie sesi lewat JavaScript lalu memasangnya di browser penyerang adalah metode klasik untuk membajak sesi korban.',
    'In practice, this approach has some significant limitations:' => 'Namun di aplikasi nyata, pencurian cookie punya beberapa batasan penting:',
    'The victim might not be logged in.' => 'Korban mungkin sedang tidak dalam keadaan login.',
    'Many applications hide their cookies from JavaScript using the [[C0]] flag.' => 'Banyak aplikasi menyembunyikan cookie sesi dari akses JavaScript lewat atribut [[C0]].',
    'Sessions might be locked to additional factors like the user\'s IP address.' => 'Sesi bisa saja terikat ke alamat IP atau sidik jari perangkat pengguna.',
    'The session might time out before you\'re able to hijack it.' => 'Sesi bisa kedaluwarsa sebelum penyerang sempat memakainya.',
    'Exploiting cross-site scripting to capture passwords' => 'Mengeksploitasi XSS untuk menangkap kata sandi',
    'These days, many users have password managers that auto-fill their passwords. You can take advantage of this by creating a password input, reading out the auto-filled password, and sending it to your own domain. This technique avoids most of the problems associated with stealing cookies, and can even gain access to every other account where the victim has reused the same password.' => 'Banyak browser modern memakai pengelola kata sandi otomatis (autofill). Skrip XSS dapat menyisipkan kolom input login palsu, menunggu browser mengisi otomatis kredensial, lalu mengirimkan username dan kata sandi tersebut ke server penyerang.',
    'The primary disadvantage of this technique is that it only works on users who have a password manager that performs password auto-fill. (Of course, if a user doesn\'t have a password saved you can still attempt to obtain their password through an on-site phishing attack, but it\'s not quite the same.)' => 'Keterbatasan teknik ini adalah hanya bekerja jika korban menyimpan kata sandinya di fitur auto-fill browser (selain opsi phishing di halaman yang sama).',
    'Exploiting cross-site scripting to bypass CSRF protections' => 'Mengeksploitasi XSS untuk melewati proteksi CSRF',
    'XSS enables an attacker to do almost anything a legitimate user can do on a website. By executing arbitrary JavaScript in a victim\'s browser, XSS allows you to perform a wide range of actions as if you were the victim user. For example, you might make a victim send a message, accept a friend request, commit a backdoor to a source code repository, or transfer some Bitcoin.' => 'Karena berjalan di dalam origin tepercaya korban, skrip XSS dapat mengirim permintaan apa pun atas nama korban: mengirim pesan, menyetujui izin, mengubah konfigurasi, hingga memindahkan aset.',
    'Some websites allow logged-in users to change their email address without re-entering their password. If you\'ve found an XSS vulnerability on one of these sites, you can exploit it to steal a CSRF token. With the token, you can change the victim\'s email address to one that you control. You can then trigger a password reset to gain access to the account.' => 'Pada situs yang mengizinkan penggantian email tanpa konfirmasi kata sandi, skrip XSS cukup membaca token anti-CSRF lalu mengirim permintaan ganti email ke alamat penyerang sebelum memicu reset kata sandi.',
    'This type of exploit combines XSS (to steal the CSRF token) with the functionality typically targeted by CSRF. While traditional CSRF is a "one-way" vulnerability, where the attacker can induce the victim to send requests but cannot see the responses, XSS enables "two-way" communication. This enables the attacker to both send arbitrary requests and read the responses, resulting in a hybrid attack that bypasses anti-CSRF defenses.' => 'Eksploitasi ini menggabungkan XSS dengan target fitur CSRF. Bila CSRF murni bersifat satu arah, XSS memungkinkan komunikasi dua arah karena skrip juga dapat membaca isi respons HTTP termasuk nilai token anti-CSRF.',
    'CSRF tokens are ineffective against XSS because XSS lets attackers read token values directly from responses.' => 'Token CSRF tidak melindungi aplikasi dari XSS karena skrip di origin yang sama tetap bebas membaca token dari DOM atau respons HTTP.',

    // preventing
    'In this section, we\'ll describe some general principles for preventing cross-site scripting vulnerabilities and ways of using various common technologies for protecting against XSS attacks.' => 'Bagian ini menjelaskan prinsip dasar pencegahan XSS serta penerapan praktisnya di berbagai teknologi web populer.',
    'Cross-site scripting prevention can generally be achieved via two layers of defense:' => 'Pencegahan XSS umumnya dibangun dengan dua lapis pertahanan utama:',
    'You can use Burp Scanner to scan your web sites for numerous security vulnerabilities including XSS. Burp\'s cutting-edge scanning logic replicates the actions of a skilled attacker and is able to achieve correspondingly high coverage of XSS vulnerabilities. You can use Burp Scanner to gain assurance that your defenses against XSS attacks are working effectively.' => 'Pengujian otomatis maupun manual secara berkala membantu memastikan seluruh mekanisme penyaringan dan encoding berjalan efektif menutup celah XSS.',
    'Learn more about Burp Scanner' => 'Pelajari pemindaian kerentanan otomatis',
    'Encoding should be applied directly before user-controllable data is written to a page, because the context you\'re writing into determines what kind of encoding you need to use. For example, values inside a JavaScript string require a different type of escaping to those in an HTML context.' => 'Encoding harus diterapkan tepat sebelum data ditulis ke halaman, karena tiap konteks (teks HTML vs literal string JavaScript) menuntut aturan escaping berbeda.',
    'In an HTML context, you should convert non-whitelisted values into HTML entities:' => 'Pada konteks HTML, karakter khusus luar daftar izin perlu diubah menjadi entitas HTML:',
    '[[C0]] converts to: [[C1]]' => '[[C0]] diubah menjadi: [[C1]]',
    'In a JavaScript string context, non-alphanumeric values should be Unicode-escaped:' => 'Pada konteks string JavaScript, karakter non-alfanumerik harus di-escape dengan format Unicode:',
    'Sometimes you\'ll need to apply multiple layers of encoding, in the correct order. For example, to safely embed user input inside an event handler, you need to deal with both the JavaScript context and the HTML context. So you need to first Unicode-escape the input, and then HTML-encode it:' => 'Terkadang diperlukan encoding berlapis sesuai urutan pemrosesan browser. Untuk menyematkan data ke dalam string JavaScript di dalam atribut event HTML, lakukan Unicode-escape lebih dulu baru kemudian HTML-encode:',
    'Encoding is probably the most important line of XSS defense, but it is not sufficient to prevent XSS vulnerabilities in every context. You should also validate input as strictly as possible at the point when it is first received from a user.' => 'Output encoding merupakan pertahanan terpenting, namun belum cukup untuk semua konteks (misalnya atribut URL). Input juga harus divalidasi seketat mungkin saat pertama kali diterima.',
    'Examples of input validation include:' => 'Contoh validasi input yang efektif meliputi:',
    'If a user submits a URL that will be returned in responses, validating that it starts with a safe protocol such as HTTP and HTTPS. Otherwise someone might exploit your site with a harmful protocol like [[C0]] or [[C1]].' => 'Saat menerima URL dari pengguna, pastikan protokolnya diawali skema aman seperti HTTP atau HTTPS agar protokol berbahaya seperti [[C0]] maupun [[C1]] tertolak.',
    'If a user supplies a value that it expected to be numeric, validating that the value actually contains an integer.' => 'Memastikan nilai yang seharusnya berupa angka benar-benar hanya berisi tipe numerik valid.',
    'Validating that input contains only an expected set of characters.' => 'Memverifikasi input hanya memuat himpunan karakter yang memang diizinkan.',
    'Input validation should ideally work by blocking invalid input. An alternative approach, of attempting to clean invalid input to make it valid, is more error prone and should be avoided wherever possible.' => 'Sebaiknya tolak langsung input yang tidak valid alih-alih mencoba membersihkan bagian berbahayanya, karena proses pembersihan rawan menyisakan celah.',
    'Input validation should generally employ whitelists rather than blacklists. For example, instead of trying to make a list of all harmful protocols ([[C0]], [[C1]], etc.), simply make a list of safe protocols (HTTP, HTTPS) and disallow anything not on the list. This will ensure your defense doesn\'t break when new harmful protocols appear and make it less susceptible to attacks that seek to obfuscate invalid values to evade a blacklist.' => 'Gunakan daftar izin (whitelist) ketimbang daftar blokir (blacklist). Menetapkan hanya skema aman seperti HTTP dan HTTPS jauh lebih kokoh dibanding mendata protokol berbahaya seperti [[C0]] dan [[C1]] yang mudah disamarkan.',
    'Allowing user-posted HTML markup' => 'Mengizinkan markup HTML dari pengguna',
    'Allowing users to post HTML markup should be avoided wherever possible, but sometimes it\'s a business requirement. For example, a blog site might allow comments to be posted containing some limited HTML markup.' => 'Hindari mengizinkan pengguna mengirim markup HTML mentah bila memungkinkan. Namun bila memang dibutuhkan secara bisnis (seperti editor artikel atau komentar terformat), penanganannya wajib sangat ketat.',
    'The classic approach is to try to filter out potentially harmful tags and JavaScript. You can try to implement this using a whitelist of safe tags and attributes, but thanks to discrepancies in browser parsing engines and quirks like mutation XSS, this approach is extremely difficult to implement securely.' => 'Menyaring tag berbahaya secara manual lewat parser buatan sendiri sangat rawan ditembus karena perbedaan parser HTML antar browser dan teknik mutation XSS.',
    'The least bad option is to use a JavaScript library that performs filtering and encoding in the user\'s browser, such as DOMPurify. Other libraries allow users to provide content in markdown format and convert the markdown into HTML. Unfortunately, all these libraries have XSS vulnerabilities from time to time, so this is not a perfect solution. If you do use one you should monitor closely for security updates.' => 'Opsi terbaik adalah memakai pustaka sanitasi tepercaya yang terawat aktif seperti DOMPurify atau mengonversi Markdown dengan sanitasi ketat, sembari terus memantau pembaruan keamanannya.',
    'In addition to JavaScript, other content such as CSS and even regular HTML can be harmful in some situations.' => 'Selain JavaScript, sisipan CSS atau HTML biasa pada situasi tertentu juga dapat memicu kebocoran data atau manipulasi antarmuka.',
    'Attacks using malicious CSS' => 'Serangan menggunakan CSS berbahaya',
    'How to prevent XSS using a template engine' => 'Cara mencegah XSS menggunakan template engine',
    'Many modern websites use server-side template engines such as Twig and Freemarker to embed dynamic content in HTML. These typically define their own escaping system. For example, in Twig, you can use the [[C0]] filter, with an argument defining the context:' => 'Banyak aplikasi modern mengandalkan template engine sisi server seperti Twig, Blade, atau Freemarker yang dilengkapi fitur auto-escaping atau filter khusus seperti [[C0]] di Twig sesuai konteksnya:',
    'Some other template engines, such as Jinja and React, escape dynamic content by default which effectively prevents most occurrences of XSS.' => 'Framework dan engine seperti Jinja, Blade, maupun React secara bawaan melakukan escaping otomatis pada ekspresi dinamis.',
    'We recommend reviewing escaping features closely when you evaluate whether to use a given template engine or framework.' => 'Selalu tinjau aturan dan pengecualian mekanisme escaping bawaan sebelum memilih sebuah template engine.',
    'If you directly concatenate user input into template strings, you will be vulnerable to [[A0]]server-side template injection[[/A0]] which is often more serious than XSS.' => 'Jangan pernah menggabungkan input pengguna langsung ke dalam string template mentah karena memicu [[A0]]server-side template injection[[/A0]] yang sering berdampak lebih parah daripada XSS.',
    'How to prevent XSS in PHP' => 'Cara mencegah XSS di PHP',
    'In PHP there is a built-in function to encode entities called [[C0]]. You should call this function to escape your input when inside an HTML context. The function should be called with three arguments:' => 'Di PHP tersedia fungsi bawaan [[C0]] (atau htmlspecialchars) untuk melakukan escaping entitas HTML dengan tiga parameter penting:',
    'Your input string.' => 'String input yang akan ditampilkan.',
    '[[C0]], which is a flag that specifies all quotes should be encoded.' => 'Flag [[C0]] agar tanda kutip ganda maupun tunggal ikut di-encode.',
    'The character set, which in most cases should be UTF-8.' => 'Pengodean karakter (charset), umumnya UTF-8.',
    'For example:' => 'Sebagai contoh:',
    'When in a JavaScript string context, you need to Unicode-escape input as already described. Unfortunately, PHP doesn\'t provide an API to Unicode-escape a string. Here is some code to do that in PHP:' => 'Pada konteks literal string JavaScript, lakukan Unicode-escape. Contoh fungsi pembantu sederhana di PHP dapat ditulis sebagai berikut:',
    'Here is how to use the [[C0]] function in PHP:' => 'Contoh pemanggilan fungsi [[C0]] tersebut di template PHP:',
    'Alternatively, you could use a template engine.' => 'Alternatif yang lebih aman adalah menggunakan template engine dengan escaping otomatis seperti Blade atau Twig.',
    'How to prevent XSS client-side in JavaScript' => 'Cara mencegah XSS di sisi klien dengan JavaScript',
    'To escape user input in an HTML context in JavaScript, you need your own HTML encoder because JavaScript doesn\'t provide an API to encode HTML. Here is some example JavaScript code that converts a string to HTML entities:' => 'Jika harus membangun HTML secara manual di JavaScript sisi klien (atau lebih baik memakai textContent), sediakan fungsi encoder entitas HTML atau gunakan API DOM aman ketimbang innerHTML:',
    'You would then use this function as follows:' => 'Contoh penggunaannya adalah sebagai berikut:',
    'If your input is inside a JavaScript string, you need an encoder that performs Unicode escaping. Here is a sample Unicode-encoder:' => 'Untuk data di dalam string JavaScript, terapkan fungsi Unicode-escape sebelum menyematkannya:',
    'How to prevent XSS in jQuery' => 'Cara mencegah XSS di jQuery',
    'The most common form of XSS in jQuery is when you pass user input to a jQuery selector. Web developers would often use [[C0]] and pass it to the selector which would cause XSS as jQuery would render the HTML. jQuery recognized this issue and patched their selector logic to check if input begins with a hash. Now jQuery will only render HTML if the first character is a [[C1]]. If you pass untrusted data to the jQuery selector, ensure you correctly escape the value using the [[C2]] function above.' => 'Sumber umum XSS di jQuery berasal dari meneruskan [[C0]] langsung ke fungsi selektor $(). Meski jQuery versi baru memperketat pencocokan dengan hanya merender HTML bila diawali karakter [[C1]], pastikan data tak tepercaya tidak pernah masuk mentah ke selektor maupun fungsi manipulasi DOM, atau terapkan sanitasi/escaping seperti [[C2]].',
    'Mitigating XSS using content security policy (CSP)' => 'Memitigasi XSS menggunakan Content Security Policy (CSP)',
    'Content security policy (CSP) is the last line of defense against cross-site scripting. If your XSS prevention fails, you can use CSP to mitigate XSS by restricting what an attacker can do.' => 'Content Security Policy (CSP) berfungsi sebagai garis pertahanan terakhir untuk memperkecil dampak serangan apabila filter dan output encoding masih tertembus.',
    'CSP lets you control various things, such as whether external scripts can be loaded and whether inline scripts will be executed. To deploy CSP you need to include an HTTP response header called [[C0]] with a value containing your policy.' => 'CSP mengatur skrip mana saja yang boleh dimuat dan dijalankan melalui header HTTP respons [[C0]].',
    'An example CSP is as follows:' => 'Contoh kebijakan CSP ketat yang umum diterapkan:',
    'This policy specifies that resources such as images and scripts can only be loaded from the same origin as the main page. So even if an attacker can successfully inject an XSS payload they can only load resources from the current origin. This greatly reduces the chance that an attacker can exploit the XSS vulnerability.' => 'Kebijakan tersebut membatasi seluruh skrip dan resource hanya dari origin yang sama, mematikan plugin objek maupun iframe berbahaya, serta membatasi URI dasar sehingga celah injeksi jauh lebih sulit dieksploitasi.',
    'If you require loading of external resources, ensure you only allow scripts that do not aid an attacker to exploit your site. For example, if you whitelist certain domains then an attacker can load any script from those domains. Where possible, try to host resources on your own domain.' => 'Jika tetap harus memuat sumber daya eksternal, pilih domain secara ketat atau host aset lokal di domain sendiri karena domain pihak ketiga yang longgar bisa disalahgunakan penyerang.',
    'If that is not possible then you can use hash- or nonce-based policy to allow scripts on different domains. A nonce is a random string that is added as an attribute of a script or resource, which will only be executed if the random string matches the server-generated one. An attacker is unable to guess the randomized string and therefore cannot invoke a script or resource with a valid nonce and so the resource will not be executed.' => 'Alternatif yang jauh lebih aman untuk skrip tepercaya lintas domain atau inline adalah memakai hash atau nonce acak per permintaan yang tidak bisa ditebak penyerang.',
    'Mitigating XSS attacks using CSP' => 'Memitigasi serangan XSS memakai CSP',
];
